	(170, 3, '2026-03-07 05:03:48', '2026-03-07 04:03:48', '', 'Dr. Anton Reinfelder', '', 'publish', 'closed', 'closed', '', 'dr-anton-reinfelder', '', '', '2026-04-27 23:30:21', '2026-04-27 21:30:21', '', 0, 'https://feboko.com/?post_type=team&#038;p=170', 14, 'team', '', 0),
	(174, 4, '2026-03-11 13:45:49', '2026-03-11 12:45:49', '<h2>India market feasibility</h2>\n<div class="css-a8ck5v css-paq0kv">\n<div class="css-a8ckwk css-paq0kv">\n\nIts more than just identifying a billion potential consumers! Entering India is a high-impact strategic decision that requires clarity, careful timing, and a realistic understanding of market dynamics. Our India Market Feasibility service supports European companies in objectively assessing whether India represents a viable and strategically aligned growth opportunity, and if so, identifying the most suitable entry route and timing. We go beyond surface-level market analysis by integrating macro-economic trends, sector and sub-sector insights, and competitive benchmarking against both global and established Indian players.\n\nThis is complemented by a detailed assessment of the regulatory, policy, and compliance landscape, as well as India-specific operational considerations that can materially impact execution and provides a data-driven roadmap for European businesses. All insights are translated into robust, scenario-based financial projections aligned with European governance standards, capital discipline, and return expectations. The outcome is a clear, evidence-driven view of opportunity, risk, and strategic fit—enabling management teams and boards to move forward with confidence, mitigate uncertainty, and take well-informed, investment-ready decisions on entering the Indian market.\n<h3>Our Focus Areas</h3>\nWe adopt a structured yet pragmatic approach, balancing analytical rigour with real-world feasibility. Our focus areas include:\n<ul>\n 	<li>Market size, growth potential, and demand drivers</li>\n 	<li>Sector and sub-sector attractiveness and opportunity mapping</li>\n 	<li>Competitive positioning versus global and Indian players</li>\n 	<li>Customer, channel, and stakeholder dynamics</li>\n 	<li>Qualitative and quantitative feasibility assessment (3-to-5-year P&amp;L projections, including realistic Capex and Opex estimates for the Indian context).</li>\n 	<li>Regulatory, policy, and compliance landscape, including FDI norms</li>\n 	<li>Evaluation of entry options (greenfield, JV, acquisition, distributor models)</li>\n 	<li>Financial modelling covering revenues, costs, breakeven, and sensitivities</li>\n 	<li>Risk–return assessment across regulatory, operational, and execution dimensions</li>\n 	<li>Evaluating industrial clusters, infrastructure quality, and state-specific incentives.</li>\n</ul>\nOur emphasis is on practical viability—ensuring that the opportunity aligns with the client’s capabilities, risk appetite, and long-term strategic objectives.\n<h3>Our Strengths</h3>\nWe bridge the gap between European ""Mittelstand"" expectations and Indian on-ground execution. Our India Market Feasibility offering is distinguished by the integration of European boardroom perspectives with deep, on-ground Indian market insight.\n<ul>\n 	<li>Strong understanding of European mid-market expectations and governance standards</li>\n 	<li>India-based specialists with cross-sector and cross-regional experience</li>\n 	<li>Proven cross-cultural expertise bridging European and Indian operating realities</li>\n 	<li>Independent, objective advice free from implementation or transaction bias</li>\n 	<li>Data-driven analysis supported by market intelligence and primary research</li>\n 	<li>Board-ready outputs designed for investment committees and senior leadership</li>\n 	<li>Practical, execution-oriented recommendations grounded in local realities</li>\n</ul>\nWe help clients avoid costly missteps and premature entry, while building a clear, defensible case for India when the opportunity is strategically and commercially sound.\n\n</div>\n<div class="css-a8ckwk css-paq0kv">\n<h2 class="css-nf5ac4 css-5ibgn5 css-w7i5ck css-g53zeq textContents">Entry Strategy &amp; Company Formation</h2>\nSetting up operations in India is a foundational decision that has long-term implications for governance, taxation, control, and operational flexibility. <strong>Choosing the right legal vehicle is the cornerstone of a successful Indian operation.</strong> Whether it is a Private Limited Subsidiary, a Liaison Office for market research, or a Joint Venture (JV) for local manufacturing, each structure carries distinct tax, compliance, and operational implications. We guide European investors through the labyrinth of the Companies Act and FEMA (Foreign Exchange Management Act) to select the optimal form. Beyond the paperwork, we manage the entire lifecycle of incorporation—from obtaining Director Identification Numbers (DIN) to drafting Articles of Association that protect the parent company’s interests. For firms considering JVs, we provide critical support in partner due diligence and the drafting of framework agreements that ensure clear exit strategies and governance control, preventing the common pitfalls of cross-border partnerships. Our company formation service extend to the point of making your legal entity fully operational by including bank account opening and obtaining requisite tax registrations which sometimes might be tricky in India due to ever changing KYC norms and government regulations.\n<h3>Our Focus Areas</h3>\nOur support covers the full lifecycle of India entry and entity establishment, with emphasis on practical and compliant structuring:\n<ul>\n 	<li>Initial Advisory: Selection of the most suitable entity type, including wholly owned subsidiary (typically a private limited company), liaison office, branch office, or LLP. Advisory on legal and tax structuring to support operational needs, profit repatriation, and scalability.</li>\n 	<li>Classical versus Fast Track Modes of Incorporations to choose from.</li>\n 	<li>Statutory Registrations: Securing PAN, TAN, GST, and Import-Export Codes (IEC) immediately post-incorporation.</li>\n 	<li>Choosing Banking Partner: Advisory on your best banking partner in India (based on the satisfaction level of our existing clients) and opening of Bank Account with complete KYC of European Shareholders</li>\n 	<li>Customization of Charter Documents: with an objective of resting the control in the hands of the Shareholders in Europe, the charter documents are customised in a manner as to render maximum efficiency with optimum governance.</li>\n 	<li>JV Frameworks: Joint venture partner due diligence, structuring shareholder agreements with a focus on intellectual property protection and management control.</li>\n</ul>\nOur focus is on creating structures that are robust, transparent, and adaptable as the business evolves.\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<h3 class="css-nf5ac4 css-5ibgn5 css-awkvn9 css-1lw1qf adjustLetterSpacing textContents">Our Strengths</h3>\nOur Entry Strategy &amp; Company Formation offering is distinguished by deep technical expertise combined with <strong>years of</strong> hands-on execution experience.\n<ul>\n 	<li>Multidisciplinary team spanning corporate law, tax, finance, and regulatory advisory</li>\n 	<li>Strong track record supporting European companies entering and scaling in India</li>\n 	<li>Extensive experience in restructuring, renegotiating, or stabilising underperforming joint ventures</li>\n 	<li>Practical understanding of shareholder protection, control mechanisms, and exit planning</li>\n 	<li>One-stop coordination with government authorities, regulators, and external stakeholders</li>\n 	<li>Independent, objective advice focused on long-term value and risk mitigation</li>\n 	<li><strong>Most importantly, transparent fee structure without any hidden costs</strong></li>\n</ul>\nWe help clients avoid structural inefficiencies and governance gaps, ensuring a smooth, well-controlled, and sustainable entry into the Indian market.\n<h2>Capital Structure &amp; Finance</h2>\nInbound investment into India is governed by a strict regulatory framework under the Reserve Bank of India (RBI) and the Foreign Exchange Management Act (FEMA). For a European parent company, funding an Indian subsidiary involves more than just a bank transfer; it requires compliance with FDI caps, valuation norms, and rigorous strict reporting timelines (such as FC-GPR filings).\n\nCapital structuring decisions in India have long-term implications for taxation, cash flows, regulatory compliance, and financial flexibility. Our Capital Structure &amp; Finance advisory supports European companies in designing financing frameworks that align with both Indian regulatory requirements and group-level funding strategies. We advise clients on the optimum combination of equity and debt instruments, intercompany funding to support initial investments as well as ongoing operations.\n\nOur approach considers not only regulatory compliance but also capital efficiency, repatriation flexibility, and risk management. We work closely with legal, tax, and finance teams to ensure that funding structures remain sustainable as the business grows. By anticipating regulatory constraints and documentation requirements upfront, we help clients avoid costly restructurings and ensure smooth execution of cross-border funding arrangements.\n<h3>Our Focus Areas</h3>\nOur work spans the full range of India-related financing considerations:\n<ul>\n 	<li>Advisory on regulatory or sectoral limits for inbound investments in India</li>\n 	<li>Foreign Direct Investment (FDI) structuring</li>\n 	<li>Intercompany loans/ External Commercial Borrowings (ECBs)</li>\n 	<li>Cross-border funding routes and capital allocation strategies</li>\n 	<li>Security packages, guarantees, and charge creation</li>\n 	<li>Review and negotiation of financing and banking documentation</li>\n 	<li>Regulatory <strong>compliances regarding</strong> foreign currency and capital flows</li>\n</ul>\nOur focus is on creating funding structures that are compliant, efficient, and future-ready.\n<h3>Our Strengths</h3>\nOur strength lies in bridging regulatory complexity with financial practicality:\n<ul>\n 	<li>Proven cross-cultural expertise across European and Indian finance environments</li>\n 	<li>Integrated legal, tax, and regulatory advisory capability</li>\n 	<li>Strong experience with regulator-driven funding structures</li>\n 	<li>Practical understanding of treasury and cash-flow considerations</li>\n 	<li>Clear, execution-focused advice for finance leadership</li>\n</ul>\nWe help clients fund Indian operations with confidence and control.\n<h2>Competitive, customer and regulatory analysis</h2>\nSuccess in India depends not only on market size, but on a clear understanding of customers, competitors, and the regulatory environment that defines the true “license to operate.” Our Competitive, Customer &amp; Regulatory Analysis service provides European companies with a structured, evidence-based view of how markets function in practice across India.\n\nWe analyse customer segments, buying behaviour, and decision-making processes to understand demand drivers and willingness to pay. In parallel, we assess the competitive landscape to identify how local and global players differentiate, price, and go to market.\n\nThis is complemented by a detailed review of sector-specific regulatory and compliance frameworks that can materially influence entry, operations, and scalability. By integrating commercial and regulatory perspectives, we help clients identify realistic differentiation levers, uncover hidden barriers, and avoid costly misjudgements—enabling informed decisions on market entry, positioning, investment priorities, and site selection.\n<h3>Our Focus Areas</h3>\nOur analysis combines market insight with regulatory clarity, focusing on both opportunity and feasibility:\n<ul>\n 	<li>Customer segmentation and demand profiling across regions and industries</li>\n 	<li>Analysis of buying behaviour, procurement practices, and decision cycles</li>\n 	<li>Competitor benchmarking covering positioning, offerings, pricing, and capabilities</li>\n 	<li>Assessment of pricing dynamics and margin structures</li>\n 	<li>Evaluation of sales, distribution, and channel strategies</li>\n 	<li>Sector-specific regulatory and compliance mapping</li>\n 	<li>Identification of operational, licensing, and approval requirements</li>\n 	<li>Assessment of barriers to entry and differentiation opportunities</li>\n</ul>\nOur focus is on translating complexity into actionable insight that supports strategic and commercial decisions.\n<h3>Our Strengths</h3>\nOur offering is distinguished by rigorous methodology combined with practical execution insight.\n<ul>\n 	<li>Proven analytical frameworks used by leading international advisory firms</li>\n 	<li>Integrated perspective across commercial, legal, tax, and regulatory dimensions</li>\n 	<li>Deep understanding of India-specific market and compliance realities</li>\n 	<li>Data-driven analysis supported by primary and secondary research</li>\n 	<li>Clear, management-ready outputs tailored for senior leadership and boards</li>\n 	<li>Practical insights that directly support investment, entry, and site-selection decisions</li>\n</ul>\nWe help clients move beyond assumptions, enabling confident positioning and compliant operations in the Indian market.\n<h2>Distribution &amp; network setup</h2>\nBuilding an effective distribution and sales network is critical to achieving sustainable growth in the Indian market. Our Distribution &amp; Network Setup service supports European companies in designing and implementing distribution architectures, sales structures, and support networks that are commercially viable, scalable, and aligned with local market realities. We begin by evaluating whether a direct or indirect sales model—or a hybrid approach—is most appropriate, taking into account product complexity, customer expectations, pricing dynamics, and regulatory considerations.\n\nBeyond identifying distributors or channel partners, we focus on creating robust go-to-market structures that ensure accountability, transparency, and long-term performance. This includes defining roles, responsibilities, and performance metrics across the network. By combining strategic design with on-ground partner validation, we help clients avoid common pitfalls such as misaligned incentives, weak coverage, or loss of control—laying the foundation for consistent market penetration and sustainable revenue growth in India.\n<h3>Our Focus Areas</h3>\nOur approach covers both strategic design and practical execution of distribution and sales networks:\n<ul>\n 	<li>Evaluation of direct, indirect, and hybrid sales models</li>\n 	<li>Design of sales structures aligned with customer segments and regions</li>\n 	<li>Identification, screening, and qualification of distributors, agents, and channel partners</li>\n 	<li>Structuring and negotiation of distribution and channel agreements</li>\n 	<li>Compliance review of contracts and channel arrangements</li>\n 	<li>Definition of performance metrics, incentives, and governance mechanisms</li>\n 	<li>Ongoing performance management, network optimisation, and realignment</li>\n</ul>\nOur focus is on building networks that are effective in practice, not just attractive on paper.\n<h3>Our Strengths</h3>\nOur Distribution &amp; Network Setup offering is distinguished by hands-on execution experience and strong local connectivity.\n<ul>\n 	<li>Access to a strong, vetted network of Indian distributors and channel partners</li>\n 	<li>Practical experience correcting or restructuring underperforming sales setups</li>\n 	<li>Deep understanding of India-specific channel dynamics and partner behaviour</li>\n 	<li>Transparent, KPI-driven governance models aligned with European headquarters</li>\n 	<li>Independent advice that prioritises long-term control and scalability</li>\n 	<li>On-ground support to validate partners and monitor early-stage performance</li>\n</ul>\nWe help clients establish distribution networks that deliver control, visibility, and sustainable growth in the Indian market.', 'India Entry & Expansion Strategy', 'Our India market entry consulting supports European companies with feasibility analysis, company formation, funding, compliance, and distribution setup for a structured and risk-aware expansion into India.', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '40-autosave-v1', '', '', '2026-03-11 13:45:49', '2026-03-11 12:45:49', '', 40, 'https://feboko.com/?p=174', 0, 'revision', '', 0),
	(175, 4, '2026-03-11 13:53:08', '2026-03-11 12:53:08', '<h2>Corporate Law</h2>\nOur Corporate Law advisory supports European companies across throughout the entire lifecycle of their Indian operations - from initial incorporation and capitalisation to growth, eventual restructuring, and exit, whenever required. We help clients establish governance structures that meet Indian legal requirements while remaining aligned with European board-level expectations and control standards.\n\nFrom the outset, we focus on establishing clear and workable structures around shareholder rights, board authority, decision-making processes, and statutory compliance. As businesses evolve, we continue to support clients through changes in ownership, capital structure, or group organisation, ensuring that legal frameworks remain robust and adaptable.\n\nWhether supporting routine compliance or complex restructuring scenarios, our advice is designed to reduce risk, enhance transparency, and enable effective oversight. By combining technical corporate law expertise with practical execution insight, we help clients operate confidently within India’s regulatory environment while preserving strategic flexibility.\n<h3>Our focus areas</h3>\nOur corporate law support is structured to address both foundational and ongoing requirements:\n<ul>\n 	<li>Corporate governance frameworks, board composition and board procedures</li>\n 	<li>Shareholder rights, reserved matters, voting mechanisms and minority protection</li>\n 	<li>Holding structures and inter-company arrangements</li>\n 	<li>Corporate secretarial services and statutory filings</li>\n 	<li>Ongoing compliance with Companies Act and allied regulations</li>\n 	<li>Special focus areas like customization of charter documents (i.e. Memorandum and Articles of Association)</li>\n 	<li>Corporate Events such dividend declaration, change of directors, change of auditor and appropriate approvals for the same</li>\n 	<li>Support during restructuring, divestments, mergers, and exits (e.g. liquidation, winding up or strike off)</li>\n</ul>\nOur focus is on building governance structures that are compliant, clear, and resilient over time and facilitate pro-active support to European Decision Makers.\n<h3>Our strengths</h3>\nOur Corporate Law offering is distinguished by deep local expertise combined with international governance understanding:\n<ul>\n 	<li>India-based specialists with cross-sector and cross-regional experience</li>\n 	<li>Strong familiarity with European governance and reporting standards</li>\n 	<li>Practical experience across the full corporate lifecycle</li>\n 	<li>Clear, board-ready advice that supports decision-making</li>\n 	<li>Proactive identification and mitigation of governance risks</li>\n</ul>\nWe help clients maintain control, transparency, and legal certainty throughout their India journey.\n<h2>Employment Law</h2>\nIndia’s employment law landscape is complex, highly regulated, and deeply influenced by local practices and cultural expectations and currently is undergoing a paradigm shift, particularly with the introduction of the new Labor Codes. Our Employment Law advisory helps European companies design people policies that are legally compliant, commercially competitive, and culturally appropriate for Indian operations.\n\nWe support clients in translating global HR principles into locally workable frameworks that minimise legal risk while supporting talent attraction and retention. Our advice covers the full employee lifecycle, from hiring and compensation structuring to workforce restructuring and separations. We place particular emphasis on managing compliance across multiple labour laws, avoiding disputes, and ensuring consistent application of policies.\n\nBy balancing regulatory requirements with operational realities, we help clients create stable employment frameworks that support growth while protecting the organisation from reputational and legal exposure.\n<h3>Our focus areas</h3>\nOur employment law support addresses both preventive compliance and risk management:\n<ul>\n 	<li>Drafting and review of employment and leadership contracts</li>\n 	<li>HR policies, employee handbooks, and workplace codes of conduct</li>\n 	<li>Advisory on the issues of Employee\'s Provident Fund, Employees\' State Insurance, Professional Tax, Labour Welfare Fund etc.</li>\n 	<li>POSH &amp; Internal Governance: Setting up Internal Committees (IC) and conducting mandatory awareness training for staff.</li>\n 	<li>Working time regulations, compensation structures, and benefits</li>\n 	<li>Terminations, redundancies, and workforce restructuring</li>\n 	<li>Industrial relations and union engagement</li>\n 	<li>Employment dispute prevention and litigation risk mitigation</li>\n</ul>\nOur focus is on creating employment frameworks that are compliant, practical, and scalable.\n<h3>Our strengths</h3>\nOur Employment Law advisory combines legal rigour with business pragmatism:\n<ul>\n 	<li>Deep understanding of Indian labour laws and enforcement practices</li>\n 	<li>Experience supporting European HR and leadership teams</li>\n 	<li>Practical, solution-oriented approach to people matters</li>\n 	<li>Strong sensitivity to cultural and workforce dynamics</li>\n 	<li>Clear guidance that balances compliance with operational flexibility</li>\n</ul>\nWe help clients manage workforce complexity while maintaining operational stability.\n<h2>Capital Structure &amp; Finance</h2>\nInbound investment into India is governed by a strict regulatory framework under the Reserve Bank of India (RBI) and the Foreign Exchange Management Act (FEMA). For a European parent company, funding an Indian subsidiary involves more than just a bank transfer; it requires compliance with FDI caps, valuation norms, and rigorous strict reporting timelines (such as FC-GPR filings).\n\nCapital structuring decisions have long-term implications for taxation, cash flows, regulatory compliance, and financial flexibility. Our Capital Structure &amp; Finance advisory supports European companies in designing financing frameworks that align with both Indian regulatory requirements and group-level funding strategies. We advise clients on the optimum combination of equity and debt instruments, intercompany funding to support initial investments as well as ongoing operations.\n\nOur approach considers not only regulatory compliance but also capital efficiency, repatriation flexibility, and risk management. We work closely with legal, tax, and finance teams to ensure that funding structures remain sustainable as the business grows. By anticipating regulatory constraints and documentation requirements upfront, we help clients avoid costly restructurings and ensure smooth execution of cross-border funding arrangements.\n<h3>Our focus areas</h3>\nOur work spans the full range of India-related financing considerations:\n<ul>\n 	<li>Advisory on regulatory or sectoral limits for inbound investments in India</li>\n 	<li>Foreign Direct Investment (FDI) structuring</li>\n 	<li>Intercompany loans/ External Commercial Borrowings (ECBs)</li>\n 	<li>Cross-border funding routes and capital allocation strategies</li>\n 	<li>Security packages, guarantees, and charge creation</li>\n 	<li>Review and negotiation of financing and banking documentation</li>\n 	<li>Regulatory compliances regarding foreign currency and capital flows</li>\n</ul>\nOur focus is on creating funding structures that are compliant, efficient, and future-ready.\n<h3>Our strenghts</h3>\nOur strength lies in bridging regulatory complexity with financial practicality:\n<ul>\n 	<li>Proven cross-cultural expertise across European and Indian finance environments</li>\n 	<li>Integrated legal, tax, and regulatory advisory capability</li>\n 	<li>Strong experience with regulator-driven funding structures</li>\n 	<li>Practical understanding of treasury and cash-flow considerations</li>\n 	<li>Clear, execution-focused advice for finance leadership</li>\n</ul>\nWe help clients fund Indian operations with confidence and control.B13\n<h2>FEMA</h2>\nIndia’s foreign exchange regulations under FEMA directly impact how capital is introduced, utilised, and repatriated. Our FEMA advisory helps European companies navigate these regulations to ensure compliant capital structuring and cross-border transactions. We support clients across inbound investments, ongoing operations, and outbound payments, ensuring alignment with evolving regulatory norms.\n\nOur approach balances strict compliance while retaining commercial flexibility, enabling clients to structure transactions efficiently without regulatory exposure. We also assist in managing reporting obligations and approvals, reducing the risk of delays or penalties. By providing clear guidance on complex exchange control rules, we help clients maintain confidence and predictability in cross-border financial flows.\n<h3>Our focus areas</h3>\nOur FEMA support covers all key regulatory touchpoints:\n<ul>\n 	<li>Inbound equity and debt structuring</li>\n 	<li>Pricing, valuation, and arm’s-length compliance</li>\n 	<li>External Commercial Borrowings (ECBs)</li>\n 	<li>Dividends, royalties, and technical-service fees</li>\n 	<li>Ongoing FEMA reporting and filings</li>\n 	<li>Advisory on repatriation and exit-related transactions</li>\n</ul>\nOur focus is on ensuring compliant and predictable cross-border transactions.\n<h3>Our Strenghts</h3>\nOur FEMA advisory is defined by independence and regulatory depth:\n<ul>\n 	<li>Objective advice free from transaction or implementation bias</li>\n 	<li>Strong understanding of Indian Central Bank (RBI) and FEMA regulations</li>\n 	<li>Experience supporting complex cross-border flows</li>\n 	<li>Ability to anticipate regulatory scrutiny and risks</li>\n 	<li>Clear, commercially grounded regulatory guidance</li>\n</ul>\nWe help clients manage foreign exchange compliance with confidence.\n<h2>Insolvency Laws</h2>\nIndia’s insolvency framework, centred on the Insolvency and Bankruptcy Code, 2016 (IBC), has fundamentally reshaped how financial distress, creditor rights, and business failure are addressed. While the IBC is designed to be time-bound and creditor-driven, its practical application requires careful navigation of procedural rules, judicial interpretations, and commercial dynamics.\n\nOur Insolvency &amp; Restructuring advisory supports European companies across the full spectrum of insolvency situations in India—whether as creditors seeking recovery, investors evaluating distressed opportunities, or group entities managing financial stress within Indian subsidiaries.\n\nWe provide strategic guidance that balances legal rights, commercial outcomes, and reputational considerations.\n<h3>Our focus areas</h3>\nOur support spans advisory, strategic, and execution-related aspects of Indian insolvency and restructuring matters, including:\n<ul>\n 	<li>Creditor strategy under the Insolvency and Bankruptcy Code (financial and operational creditors)</li>\n 	<li>Filing, defence, and management of insolvency proceedings before the National Company Law Tribunal (NCLT)</li>\n 	<li>Representation and strategy for participation in Committees of Creditors (CoC)</li>\n 	<li>Assessment and enforcement of security interests and guarantees</li>\n 	<li>Evaluation of resolution plans and distressed investment opportunities</li>\n 	<li>Support in out-of-court restructuring, settlements, and negotiated exits</li>\n 	<li>Cross-border considerations involving Indian insolvency proceedings</li>\n 	<li>Advisory on liquidation, dissolution, and recovery mechanisms</li>\n</ul>\nOur focus is on maximising recovery, preserving value, and enabling informed decision-making throughout the insolvency lifecycle.\n<h3>Our strenghts</h3>\nOur Insolvency &amp; Restructuring practice is distinguished by a pragmatic, commercially aligned approach:\n<ul>\n 	<li>Strong understanding of the IBC framework and evolving judicial trends</li>\n 	<li>Experience advising international creditors, investors, and group companies</li>\n 	<li>Strategic coordination with insolvency professionals, local counsel, and financial advisors</li>\n 	<li>Clear, time-sensitive advice tailored for boards, lenders, and senior management</li>\n 	<li>Emphasis on outcome-driven strategies rather than procedural formality</li>\n</ul>\nWe help clients navigate financial distress in India with clarity, control, and confidence—whether the objective is recovery, resolution, or exit.\n<h2>Intellectual Property Rights (IPR)</h2>\nProtecting intellectual property in India requires a clear understanding of local registration regimes, enforcement mechanisms, and practical market realities. While India offers a comprehensive statutory framework for patents, trademarks, designs, and copyrights, effective protection depends on timely structuring, accurate filings, and proactive enforcement strategies.\n\nOur Intellectual Property Rights advisory supports European companies in securing, managing, and enforcing their IP assets in India. We help clients align global IP strategies with Indian legal requirements, mitigate infringement risks, and preserve the commercial value of innovation, brands, and proprietary know-how across the Indian market.\n<h3>Our focus areas</h3>\nOur IPR support covers both strategic and operational aspects of IP protection and enforcement in India, including:\n<ul>\n 	<li>Registration and prosecution of patents, trademarks, designs, and copyrights</li>\n 	<li>IP portfolio structuring and alignment with group-level IP strategies</li>\n 	<li>IP due diligence for investments, acquisitions, and collaborations</li>\n 	<li>Drafting and review of IP licensing, assignment, and technology transfer agreements</li>\n 	<li>Protection of trade secrets, confidential information, and know-how</li>\n 	<li>Monitoring, enforcement, and infringement response strategies</li>\n 	<li>Support in opposition, cancellation, and rectification proceedings</li>\n 	<li>Coordination of civil, criminal, and administrative enforcement actions</li>\n</ul>\nOur focus is on safeguarding IP assets while enabling commercialisation and scalable operations in India.\n<h3>Our Strenghts</h3>\nOur Intellectual Property practice is distinguished by a combination of legal precision and commercial awareness:\n<ul>\n 	<li>Deep understanding of Indian IP laws and administrative procedures</li>\n 	<li>Experience advising European companies across technology, manufacturing, and consumer sectors</li>\n 	<li>Practical, business-oriented approach to IP protection and enforcement</li>\n 	<li>Close coordination with technical experts, enforcement agencies, and local counsel</li>\n 	<li>Clear, actionable advice for management and innovation teams</li>\n</ul>\nWe help clients protect innovation, strengthen brand integrity, and maintain competitive advantage in the Indian market.\n<h2>Antitrust &amp; Competition</h2>\nCompetition law risks in India can arise from routine commercial arrangements such as distribution models, pricing strategies, and cooperation with partners. Our Antitrust &amp; Competition advisory helps clients assess and mitigate these risks before they escalate into regulatory scrutiny or enforcement action. We provide preventive guidance tailored to Indian competition law and enforcement trends.\n\nOur support enables companies to design compliant commercial structures while preserving competitive flexibility. We also assist clients in preparing for regulatory investigations and responding effectively if issues arise. By embedding competition compliance into commercial decision-making, we help clients operate confidently and sustainably in the Indian market.\n<h3>Our focus areas</h3>\nOur competition law support focuses on risk prevention and preparedness:\n\n- Review of distribution and vertical agreements\n\n- Assessment of exclusivity and cooperation arrangements\n\n- Cartel and abuse-of-dominance risk analysis\n\n- Dawn-raid preparedness and internal protocols\n\n- Competition-compliant pricing, discounts, and rebates\n\n- Training and awareness for commercial teams\n\nOur focus is on reducing exposure while enabling compliant growth.\n<h3>Our Strenghts</h3>\nOur Antitrust &amp; Competition advisory combines legal insight with practical risk management:\n\n- Strong understanding of Indian competition law enforcement trends\n\n- Preventive, compliance-led advisory approach\n\n- Experience advising on complex distribution models\n\n- Clear, management-ready guidance for commercial teams\n\n- Ability to translate legal risk into business action\n\nWe help clients stay competitive without crossing regulatory boundaries.', 'Legal Advisory', 'Our India legal advisory supports European companies across corporate law, employment law, FEMA, capital structuring, insolvency, intellectual property, and competition matters with practical, compliant, and board-ready guidance for Indian operations.', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '109-autosave-v1', '', '', '2026-03-11 13:53:08', '2026-03-11 12:53:08', '', 109, 'https://feboko.com/?p=175', 0, 'revision', '', 0),
	(176, 4, '2026-03-11 15:50:03', '2026-03-11 14:50:03', '<h2>Accounting &amp; Financial Reporting</h2>\nAccurate and timely financial reporting is the foundation of effective management and group-level transparency. Our Accounting &amp; Financial Reporting services ensure accurate, timely and compliant financial information for Indian entities, fully aligned with group reporting requirements. We support clients from initial bookkeeping setup through ongoing monthly, quarterly and annual reporting. Particular emphasis is placed on consistency, audit readiness and transparency for headquarters and group controllers.\n\nWe bridge Indian statutory requirements with international reporting standards, enabling management to rely on financial data for decision-making rather than treating reporting as a compliance exercise. Our approach combines strong technical accounting with disciplined processes and clear ownership, reducing dependency on individuals and avoiding year-end surprises.\n<h3>Our focus areas</h3>\nOur accounting and reporting support is structured and reliable:\n<ul>\n 	<li>- Liberty of chosing the accounting system - SAP / Tally / MS Dynamics / QuickBooks</li>\n 	<li>- Statutory accounting under Indian GAAP and international standards like IFRS or European local GAAPs</li>\n 	<li>- Group reporting and consolidation support</li>\n 	<li>- Month-end and year-end closing processes</li>\n 	<li>- Chart of accounts and reporting templates aligned with group requirements</li>\n 	<li>- Statutory audit coordination and support at local level and cordination with the group auditor, if required</li>\n 	<li>- Management reporting and MIS</li>\n 	<li>- Documentation and audit trails</li>\n</ul>\nOur focus is predictable, decision-useful reporting.\n<h3>Our strengths</h3>\nWe deliver clarity and confidence in numbers:\n<ul>\n 	<li>- Alignment with European reporting expectations</li>\n 	<li>- Strong control over closing timelines</li>\n 	<li>- Robust documentation and reconciliations</li>\n 	<li>Experienced interface with auditors</li>\n 	<li>Scalable processes as volumes grow</li>\n 	<li>Clear communication with HQ finance teams</li>\n 	<li>Reduced risk of reporting surprises</li>\n</ul>\nWe make Indian reporting dependable for headquarters.\n<h2>Corporate Secretarial Compliances</h2>\nIndian corporate law involves a heavy burden of mandatory filings and statutory documentation that can be overwhelming for foreign investors. Our Corporate Secretarial Compliance service ensures that your Indian entity stays in perfect standing with the Registrar of Companies (ROC) and the Ministry of Corporate Affairs. We manage all board and shareholder meeting protocols, from drafting agendas and minutes to filing annual returns and financial statements in the required formats. Beyond routine filings, we provide strategic support for changes in capital structure, director appointments, and the maintenance of essential statutory registers. Our team acts as a proactive compliance partner, providing "compliance alerts" and managing the regulatory calendar so that your local directors and the parent company are never caught off-guard by missing a deadline. This service is essential for maintaining the legal integrity of your investment and protecting the personal liability of your board members.\n<h3>Our focus areas</h3>\nOur secretarial support is governance-driven:\n<ul>\n 	<li>Statutory filings and registers</li>\n 	<li>Board and shareholder meetings</li>\n 	<li>Resolutions and minutes</li>\n 	<li>Director and shareholding changes</li>\n 	<li>Regulatory disclosures</li>\n 	<li>Compliance calendars and tracking</li>\n 	<li>Coordination with regulators</li>\n 	<li>Event based filings and compliances (Capital Infusion, Shifting of Registered Office, Extraordinary Meetings etc.)</li>\n</ul>\nOur focus is clean governance records.\n<h3>Our strengths</h3>\nWe deliver precision and reliability:\n<ul>\n 	<li>Deep knowledge of Indian corporate law</li>\n 	<li>Strong documentation discipline</li>\n 	<li>Alignment with European governance standards</li>\n 	<li>Proactive compliance monitoring</li>\n 	<li>Clear communication with boards</li>\n 	<li>Reduced regulatory and reputational risk</li>\n 	<li>Seamless coordination with legal and tax</li>\n</ul>\nWe ensure governance stands up to scrutiny.\n<h2>Payroll &amp; Compliance</h2>\nPayroll in India involves complex labour laws, frequent regulatory changes and high employee sensitivity. Our Payroll Management services provide accurate, compliant and confidential payroll operations while ensuring a positive employee experience. We handle the entire employee lifecycle—from onboarding to final settlement—including the management of Provident Fund (PF), Employee State Insurance (ESI), and Professional Tax (PT). We also specialize in managing the tax withholdings (TDS) for both local staff and expatriate executives, ensuring that complex compensation structures are handled with complete confidentiality.\n\nOur services are designed to integrate seamlessly with HR, finance and tax processes, ensuring consistency across employment contracts, compensation structures and statutory compliance. By combining technical accuracy with process discipline, we help clients avoid compliance risks and employee dissatisfaction.\n<h3>Our focus areas</h3>\nOur payroll services are compliance-driven:\n<ul>\n 	<li>Monthly payroll processing</li>\n 	<li>Statutory Contributions: Handling all filings and payments for EPF, ESI, LWF, and other mandatory social security schemes</li>\n 	<li>Tax Withholdings (TDS): Ensuring accurate calculation and timely filing of income tax deductions for all employees</li>\n 	<li>Expat Compensation: Providing specialized support for the unique tax and social security needs of foreign nationals in India</li>\n 	<li>Leave, bonus and variable-pay handling</li>\n 	<li>Payslips and employee reporting</li>\n 	<li>Payroll reconciliations and audits</li>\n 	<li>Transition support during growth</li>\n</ul>\nOur focus is error-free and compliant payroll.\n<h3>Our strengths</h3>\nWe bring control and trust to payroll:\n<ul>\n 	<li>Strong understanding of Indian labour laws</li>\n 	<li>Secure and confidential processes</li>\n 	<li>Integration with accounting and tax</li>\n 	<li>Consistent handling of audits and inspections</li>\n 	<li>Clear escalation and issue resolution</li>\n 	<li>Reliable service continuity</li>\n 	<li>Reduced employee and compliance risk</li>\n</ul>\nWe ensure payroll runs smoothly - every month.\n<h2>Banking</h2>\nEfficient banking arrangements are critical for smooth financial operations in India. Our Banking advisory supports European companies in choosing the correct banking partners and managing the process of opening and operationalising bank accounts in India. We guide clients through documentation, regulatory requirements, and coordination with banks to ensure timely and compliant account setup.\n\nBeyond basic account opening, we advise on structuring banking arrangements that support treasury operations, foreign currency transactions, and operational needs. Our support ensures that banking frameworks are aligned with regulatory requirements while remaining practical for day-to-day business operations. By reducing delays and friction with financial institutions, we help clients establish stable and reliable banking foundations from the outset.\n<h3>Our focus areas</h3>\nOur banking support combines regulatory understanding with execution assistance:\n<ul>\n 	<li>Selection of Indian and international banking partners</li>\n 	<li>Support in opening and operationalising bank accounts including support in activation of internet banking feature under "four eyes principle" of maker and authorizor</li>\n 	<li>Advisory on opening and operating the special accounts such as EEFC and other permitted structures</li>\n 	<li>Assistance with KYC, documentation, and compliance processes</li>\n 	<li>Coordination with banks on transaction and reporting requirements</li>\n 	<li>Support for treasury and cash-management needs</li>\n</ul>\nOur focus is on enabling smooth, compliant, and efficient banking operations.\n<h3>Our strengths</h3>\nOur Banking advisory is grounded in hands-on execution experience:\n<ul>\n 	<li>Practical understanding of Indian banking procedures</li>\n 	<li>Our Expert Team boasts of former Bankers</li>\n 	<li>Strong working relationships with major Indian banks</li>\n 	<li>Experience navigating complex KYC and documentation requirements</li>\n 	<li>Execution-focused support for finance and treasury teams</li>\n 	<li>Ability to resolve delays and operational bottlenecks</li>\n</ul>\nWe help clients establish reliable banking operations without unnecessary friction.\n<h2>BPO Services</h2>\nFor growing subsidiaries in India, building a full-scale administrative team can be a distraction from core business activities. Our Business Process Outsourcing (BPO) services allow you to scale your operations by outsourcing essential back-office functions to our expert team. We provide a single point of contact for multiple administrative tasks, including expense management, vendor coordination, and the management of corporate insurance policies. Our service levels are flexible, allowing you to increase or decrease support as your Indian entity evolves from a small representative office to a large manufacturing hub. We apply European management standards to these outsourced functions, ensuring a level of quality and cost-transparency that is often difficult to find in the local market. By leveraging our BPO services, you can maintain a "lean" local organization while benefiting from professional, high-standard administrative support.\n<h3>Our focus areas</h3>\nOur BPO services cover core processes and are scalable:\n<ul>\n 	<li>Administrative Support: Handling day-to-day back-office tasks, allowing your local team to focus on sales and production (e.g., managing travel bookings, card printing etc)</li>\n 	<li>Expense Management: Managing employee reimbursements and corporate travel expenses according to your global policies.</li>\n 	<li>Insurance Management: Coordinating the procurement and renewal of essential business and employee insurance policies.</li>\n 	<li>Scalable Solutions: Our services grow with your business, from a two-person sales office to a full-scale manufacturing plant.</li>\n</ul>\nOur focus is scalable, controlled finance operations.\n<h3>Our strengths</h3>\nWe combine efficiency with governance and provide a single point of contact for multiple back-office functions, combining European management standards with Indian cost advantages. Our flexible service levels are designed to support subsidiaries throughout their growth stages.\n<h2>Cash, Treasury &amp; Banking Support</h2>\nManaging cash and banking in India requires close attention to regulatory, tax and operational considerations. Our Cash and Treasury services are designed to help you design and maintain efficient cash-management processes tailored to both local realities and your global group requirements. We assist in cash-flow forecasting to ensure that your Indian subsidiary always has the liquidity needed for its operations while minimizing idle cash. We also manage your relationships with local banks, ensuring you get the best terms for your deposits and credit lines. Our Cash, Treasury &amp; Banking Support services help clients establish efficient cash-management structures while maintaining compliance with foreign-exchange and banking regulations.\n<h3>Our focus areas</h3>\nOur treasury support is control-oriented:\n<ul>\n 	<li>Bank account setup and management</li>\n 	<li>Payment and approval workflows</li>\n 	<li>Cash-flow forecasting and monitoring</li>\n 	<li>FX and repatriation planning</li>\n 	<li>Intercompany funding structures</li>\n 	<li>Regulatory compliance support</li>\n 	<li>Banking relationship management</li>\n</ul>\nOur focus is liquidity with compliance.\n<h3>Our strengths</h3>\nWe bring discipline to cash management:\n<ul>\n 	<li>Strong understanding of Indian banking practices</li>\n 	<li>Alignment with group treasury policies</li>\n 	<li>Clear controls and approval matrices</li>\n 	<li>Practical handling of FX regulations</li>\n 	<li>Predictable cash-flow visibility</li>\n 	<li>Reduced operational and compliance risk</li>\n 	<li>Reliable coordination with banks</li>\n</ul>\nWe help clients stay liquid and compliant.', 'Finance, Accounting & Business Administration', 'Our India finance and accounting services support European companies with financial reporting, corporate secretarial compliance, payroll, banking, BPO, and treasury processes through compliant, scalable, and execution-focused support for Indian operations.', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '113-autosave-v1', '', '', '2026-03-11 15:50:03', '2026-03-11 14:50:03', '', 113, 'https://feboko.com/?p=176', 0, 'revision', '', 0),
	(177, 4, '2026-03-11 14:13:02', '2026-03-11 13:13:02', '<h2>Corporate Tax Advisory</h2>\nA robust tax strategy is essential for protecting the profitability of your Indian investment and ensuring long-term compliance across borders. Our Corporate Tax Advisory services support European companies in structuring and managing their Indian corporate tax positions in a manner that is efficient, transparent, and fully compliant across jurisdictions. We advise across the full lifecycle—from initial investment structuring to ongoing operations, profit repatriation, and eventual restructuring or exit. Our approach balances Indian tax law, international tax principles, and treaty frameworks with European group objectives, ensuring alignment between local execution and global tax strategy.\n\nWe focus on creating defensible structures that withstand regulatory scrutiny while remaining practical to operate. This includes evaluating holding and operating structures, optimising cash repatriation mechanisms, and managing effective tax rates without introducing undue complexity or risk. Particular attention is given to documentation, audit readiness, and consistency with group tax positions. The outcome is a coherent Indian tax framework that supports business growth, meets governance expectations, and enables informed decision-making by group tax teams and boards.\n<h3>Our focus areas</h3>\nOur corporate tax work is anchored in strategic alignment and regulatory certainty:\n<ul>\n 	<li>Investment and holding-structure optimisation</li>\n 	<li>Treaty analysis and cross-border tax alignment</li>\n 	<li>Profit repatriation planning (dividends, fees, royalties)</li>\n 	<li>Effective tax-rate management and modelling</li>\n 	<li>Documentation aligned with group tax policies</li>\n 	<li>Audit and scrutiny preparedness</li>\n 	<li>Coordination with international tax advisors</li>\n</ul>\nOur focus is on sustainable, defensible tax outcomes—not short-term optimisation.\n<h3>Our strengths</h3>\nOur strength lies in combining technical depth with group-level clarity:\n<ul>\n 	<li>Senior tax professionals with international experience</li>\n 	<li>Strong understanding of European group tax governance</li>\n 	<li>Clear, well-reasoned written opinions for group files</li>\n 	<li>Practical structuring grounded in Indian realities</li>\n 	<li>Consistent positions across years and entities</li>\n 	<li>Close coordination with headquarters tax teams</li>\n 	<li>Proactive risk identification and mitigation</li>\n</ul>\nWe help clients manage Indian tax exposure with confidence and control.\n<h2>Indirect Tax</h2>\nIndia’s indirect tax framework - particularly GST - has a direct impact on pricing, margins, working capital, and operational efficiency. Our Indirect Tax services support clients in designing, reviewing, and stabilising GST and other indirect-tax processes to ensure smooth operations, accurate credit utilisation, and minimal disputes. We work closely with finance, logistics, and supply-chain teams to ensure tax processes reflect commercial reality and operational flows.\n\nOur advisory goes beyond registrations and returns. We analyse supply chains, transaction flows, and documentation to identify risks, inefficiencies, and blocked credits. We also support clients during audits, assessments, and departmental inquiries, helping them respond with clarity and consistency. By embedding indirect-tax considerations into day-to-day processes, we help clients reduce friction, improve predictability, and avoid downstream litigation. The result is a GST framework that supports business continuity while remaining compliant across multiple states and operational models.\n<h3>Our focus areas</h3>\nOur indirect-tax support is practical and process-driven:\n<ul>\n 	<li>GST registration, classification, and rate analysis</li>\n 	<li>Supply-chain and transaction tax mapping</li>\n 	<li>Input-tax credit (ITC) optimisation and reviews</li>\n 	<li>Advisory on complex topics of export / import of goods and services under GST and other transaction advisory</li>\n 	<li>GST health checks and risk diagnostics</li>\n 	<li>Audit support and representation before authorities</li>\n 	<li>Multi-state compliance coordination</li>\n</ul>\nOur focus is on prevention, accuracy, and operational continuity.\n<h3>Our strengths</h3>\nWe bring execution realism to indirect-tax advisory:\n<ul>\n 	<li>Process-oriented approach integrating tax, finance, and logistics</li>\n 	<li>Experience with complex, multi-state operations</li>\n 	<li>Early-warning mindset to prevent disputes</li>\n 	<li>Strong audit-handling and representation capability</li>\n 	<li>Clear documentation and reconciliations</li>\n 	<li>Practical guidance rather than theoretical positions</li>\n 	<li>Consistent support during audits and assessments</li>\n</ul>\nWe help clients make GST work for the business - not against it.\n<h2>Direct Tax</h2>\nOur Direct Tax services cover all aspects of Indian corporate income taxation, providing end-to-end support from return preparation to assessments, audits, and appellate proceedings. We assist clients in navigating India’s evolving tax landscape while maintaining consistency with global tax policies and audit standards. Our work is grounded in accuracy, defensibility, and disciplined documentation.\n\nWe support tax computations, filings, withholding-tax obligations, and provisioning, while also representing clients during tax scrutinies and inquiries. Special emphasis is placed on preparing robust documentation and audit trails that withstand regulatory review and align with group audit expectations. By maintaining consistent methodologies across years and entities, we help clients reduce volatility, manage exposure, and avoid surprises. The outcome is a stable, well-managed direct-tax position that allows management to focus on operations rather than uncertainty.\n<h3>Our focus areas</h3>\nOur direct-tax services are structured for consistency and control:\n<ul>\n 	<li>Corporate tax computations and return filings</li>\n 	<li>Withholding-tax advisory and compliance including on cross boarder transactions</li>\n 	<li>Tax provisioning and reporting support</li>\n 	<li>Handling of assessments / scrutinies and enquiries</li>\n 	<li>Representation in appeals and proceedings</li>\n 	<li>Documentation and audit preparedness</li>\n 	<li>Coordination with statutory and group auditors</li>\n</ul>\nOur focus is on predictability and defensibility.\n<h3>Our strenghts</h3>\nWe deliver reliability in a complex tax environment:\n<ul>\n 	<li>Consistent methodology across years and entities</li>\n 	<li>Documentation aligned with global audit requirements</li>\n 	<li>Responsive support during assessments and appeals</li>\n 	<li>Clear articulation of positions to authorities</li>\n 	<li>Strong coordination with finance and audit teams</li>\n 	<li>Practical risk assessment and mitigation</li>\n 	<li>Long-term continuity of advice</li>\n</ul>\nWe ensure Indian direct tax remains controlled and manageable.\n<h2>Transfer Pricing</h2>\nTransfer pricing is a key risk area for multinational groups operating in India. Our Transfer Pricing services help clients design, implement, and defend pricing models that reflect commercial reality and withstand regulatory scrutiny. We focus on aligning inter-company arrangements with actual functions, risks, and value creation in India, while remaining consistent with global TP frameworks.\n\nWe support clients across the full TP lifecycle—from functional and economic analysis to benchmarking, documentation, and audit defence. Particular emphasis is placed on dispute prevention through robust upfront design and clear documentation. Where disputes arise, we assist in managing audits and negotiations with tax authorities. Our approach balances economic rigour with practical operability, ensuring TP policies are not only defensible but also workable for business teams.\n<h3>Our focus areas</h3>\nOur TP work is grounded in substance and clarity:\n<ul>\n 	<li>Functional, asset, and risk (FAR) analyses</li>\n 	<li>Benchmarking and full scale Transfer Pricing Studies</li>\n 	<li>Inter-company pricing policies</li>\n 	<li>Master file and local file documentation</li>\n 	<li>Audit and scrutiny support</li>\n 	<li>Dispute-prevention strategies</li>\n 	<li>Alignment with global TP frameworks</li>\n</ul>\nOur focus is on reducing controversy while supporting business models.\n<h3>Our strenghts</h3>\nWe combine technical depth with commercial understanding:\n<ul>\n 	<li>Integrated teams of economists and tax experts</li>\n 	<li>Experience with European Mittelstand and large groups</li>\n 	<li>Strong focus on dispute prevention</li>\n 	<li>Clear, defensible documentation</li>\n 	<li>Practical solutions aligned with operations</li>\n 	<li>Effective audit and inquiry handling</li>\n 	<li>Consistency with OECD and EU expectations</li>\n</ul>\nWe help clients manage TP as a governance issue, not just a tax risk.\n<h2>Tax Compliance Services</h2>\nTax compliance in India involves multiple filings, payments, reconciliations, and procedural requirements across direct and indirect taxes. Our Tax Compliance Services provide operational support to ensure all statutory obligations are met accurately and on time, allowing management to focus on business priorities. We act as a central coordination point, integrating compliance across tax types and entities.\n\nWe manage recurring filings, payment tracking, documentation, and reconciliations while maintaining visibility for group finance and tax teams. Our structured processes, digital workflows, and reminder systems reduce dependency on individuals and minimise the risk of missed deadlines. The result is a stable compliance environment with clear accountability, reliable reporting, and audit-ready documentation.\n<h3>Our focus areas</h3>\nOur compliance support is disciplined and system-driven:\n<ul>\n 	<li>Direct and indirect tax returns for Indian and overseas entities</li>\n 	<li>Payment tracking, reconciliations and coordination for refunds</li>\n 	<li>Documentation and record management</li>\n 	<li>Compliance calendars and reminders</li>\n 	<li>Coordination with statutory auditors</li>\n 	<li>Query handling and follow-ups</li>\n 	<li>Dashboard reporting for management</li>\n</ul>\nOur focus is reliability and consistency.\n<h3>Our strengths</h3>\nWe bring structure to routine compliance:\n<ul>\n 	<li>Integrated tax and BPO delivery teams</li>\n 	<li>Digital workflows and tracking tools</li>\n 	<li>Reliable deadline management</li>\n 	<li>Clear ownership and accountability</li>\n 	<li>Strong audit and review readiness</li>\n 	<li>Scalable processes as operations grow</li>\n 	<li>Transparent reporting to headquarters</li>\n</ul>\nWe ensure compliance becomes routine - not a risk.\n<h2>Permanent Establishment</h2>\nThe risk of creating a Permanent Establishment in India is a critical concern for foreign companies operating through sales, service, or project models. We provide strategic advisory on whether your overseas business structures—such as sales models, service projects, or temporary assignments—accidentally create a taxable presence (PE) in India. This is a common trap that can lead to significant back-taxes and penalties. We review your contracts and operational models to document the functions being performed, helping you limit your exposure while enabling your business to operate effectively. Our integrated approach ensures that your Indian entity is both compliant on the surface and structurally protected against complex international tax risks.\n<h3>Our focus areas</h3>\nOur PE services focus on clarity and mitigation:\n<ul>\n 	<li>PE risk reviews for sales and service models</li>\n 	<li>Project-based PE assessments</li>\n 	<li>Treaty interpretation and documentation</li>\n 	<li>Functional analysis and evidence creation</li>\n 	<li>Registration and filing support for foreign entities for tax purposes if a project-specific presence is required</li>\n 	<li>Alignment with global tax positions</li>\n 	<li>Risk-mitigation strategies</li>\n</ul>\nOur focus is enabling business while managing exposure.\n<h3>Our strengths</h3>\nWe bring international perspective to PE analysis:\n<ul>\n 	<li>Deep knowledge of treaties and global practice</li>\n 	<li>Experience with European operating models</li>\n 	<li>Practical, business-friendly solutions</li>\n 	<li>Clear documentation for audits</li>\n 	<li>Strong coordination with global tax advisors</li>\n 	<li>Balanced risk-reward assessment</li>\n 	<li>Credible positions with authorities</li>\n</ul>\nWe help clients operate in India without unintended tax consequences.\n<h2>Taxes for Ex-pats</h2>\nManaging expatriate and cross-border employee taxation requires close coordination between tax, HR, and payroll functions. Our Expat Tax services support companies and individuals in navigating Indian tax, social security, and compliance requirements while maintaining alignment with home-country obligations. We focus on clarity, predictability, and employee confidence.\n\nWe advise on compensation structuring, withholding optimisation, tax equalisation policies, and social-security considerations. Our approach ensures employees understand their obligations and benefits, reducing uncertainty and disputes. By coordinating with HR and payroll teams, we help clients implement compliant and employee-friendly solutions that support mobility and retention.\n<h3>Our focus areas</h3>\nOur expat tax support is integrated and employee-centric:\n<ul>\n 	<li>Compensation and assignment structuring</li>\n 	<li>Tax withholding and reporting</li>\n 	<li>Equalisation and protection policies</li>\n 	<li>Social-security analysis</li>\n 	<li>Cross-border commuter issues</li>\n 	<li>Employee communication and support</li>\n 	<li>Coordination with payroll and HR</li>\n</ul>\nOur focus is smooth mobility with controlled tax outcomes.\n<h3>Our strengths</h3>\nWe bridge tax rules and people realities:\n<ul>\n 	<li>Close cooperation between tax and HR specialists</li>\n 	<li>Experience with German and wider European rules</li>\n 	<li>Clear communication to employees and management</li>\n 	<li>Practical implementation support</li>\n 	<li>Alignment with global mobility policies</li>\n 	<li>Reduced risk of employee disputes</li>\n 	<li>Trusted advisory relationship</li>\n</ul>\nWe make cross-border mobility predictable and compliant.\n<h2>Indian Customs</h2>\nOur Indian Customs advisory supports clients in managing valuation, classification, and procedural aspects of imports into India, including related-party transactions. We help clients navigate complex customs regulations while maintaining operational efficiency and compliance.\n\nWe assist with HS classification, valuation methods, and special regimes, and support interactions with customs authorities during audits and inquiries. Our approach integrates legal, tax, and operational perspectives to ensure positions are defensible and workable. The outcome is reduced clearance risk, predictable duty exposure, and smoother import operations.\n<h3>Our focus areas</h3>\nOur customs services focus on accuracy and defence:\n<ul>\n 	<li>- HS classification analysis</li>\n 	<li>- Customs valuation and related-party pricing</li>\n 	<li>- Special regimes and exemptions</li>\n 	<li>- Documentation and procedural compliance</li>\n 	<li>- Audit and inquiry support</li>\n 	<li>- Interaction with customs authorities</li>\n 	<li>- Risk assessment and mitigation</li>\n</ul>\nOur focus is predictability and control at the border.\n<h3>Our strengths</h3>\nWe combine technical depth with operational insight:\n\n- Strong track record with manufacturing and trading clients\n\n- Integrated legal, tax, and operational view\n\n- Experience in customs audits and investigations\n\n- Clear, defensible documentation\n\n- Practical solutions for ongoing operations\n\n- Responsive support during inquiries\n\n- Credible engagement with authorities\n\nWe help clients keep goods moving - without surprises.', 'Tax Advisory', 'Our India tax advisory supports European companies across corporate tax, GST, direct tax, transfer pricing, tax compliance, permanent establishment, expatriate tax, and customs with practical, defensible, and cross-border aligned guidance for Indian operations.', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '115-autosave-v1', '', '', '2026-03-11 14:13:02', '2026-03-11 13:13:02', '', 115, 'https://feboko.com/?p=177', 0, 'revision', '', 0),
	(178, 4, '2026-03-11 14:19:41', '2026-03-11 13:19:41', '<h2>Site Selection &amp; Location Advisory</h2>\nSelecting the right location in India is a strategic decision with long-term implications for cost, talent access, regulatory exposure and operational scalability. Our Site Selection &amp; Location Advisory service supports European companies in identifying and evaluating optimal locations for manufacturing units, offices, R&amp;D centres or shared services operations.\n\nWe go beyond headline cost comparisons to assess infrastructure readiness, logistics connectivity, talent availability, regulatory environment, incentive regimes and ecosystem maturity. We conduct an independent assessment free of local vendor interests, focusing on regions that offer the best "proximity to ports" or industrial clusters for your specific sector. Our analysis balances short-term setup efficiency with long-term sustainability, ensuring that location decisions support growth rather than constrain it. Outputs are designed to support board and investment committee decisions with clear trade-offs and recommendations.\n<h3>Our focus areas</h3>\nOur approach is analytical and practical:\n<ul>\n 	<li>Multi-city and multi-state shortlisting</li>\n 	<li>Cost benchmarking (real estate, labour, utilities), promimity to ports - highly relevant for manufacturing and trading firms</li>\n 	<li>Talent pool and skill availability analysis</li>\n 	<li>Infrastructure and logistics assessment, Industrial Park Reviews</li>\n 	<li>Analyzing the availability of skilled labor and the quality of transport links in target regions</li>\n 	<li>State incentives and policy evaluation</li>\n 	<li>Regulatory and compliance considerations</li>\n 	<li>Site visits and stakeholder interactions</li>\n</ul>\nOur focus is on locations that work in practice.\n<h3>Our strengths</h3>\nWe bring clarity to complex choices:\n<ul>\n 	<li>Deep, on-ground regional knowledge</li>\n 	<li>Neutral, data-driven recommendations</li>\n 	<li>Experience across industrial and service sectors</li>\n 	<li>Integration with tax and regulatory advice</li>\n 	<li>Clear comparison frameworks for boards</li>\n 	<li>Risk-aware location selection</li>\n 	<li>Long-term scalability lens</li>\n</ul>\nWe help clients choose locations with confidence.\n<h2>Operations Setup &amp; Scale Up</h2>\nSetting up operations in India requires careful orchestration across legal, regulatory, people and infrastructure dimensions. Our Operations Setup &amp; Scale-Up services support clients from initial establishment through stabilisation and growth with "boots on the ground" approach needed to manage the ramp-up of your facility or office.\n\nWe help design operating models, set up facilities, implement internal controls and establish management processes that align with group standards while remaining suited to Indian realities. Our focus is on speed, compliance and operational resilience—ensuring clients move from “setup” to “business-as-usual” efficiently and without disruption.\n<h3>Our focus areas</h3>\nOur support is end-to-end:\n<ul>\n 	<li>Operating model and organisation design</li>\n 	<li>Facility and vendor onboarding</li>\n 	<li>Internal controls and SOP development</li>\n 	<li>Compliance and reporting frameworks</li>\n 	<li>Management cadence and KPIs</li>\n 	<li>Cost and efficiency optimisation</li>\n 	<li>Scale-up readiness assessment</li>\n</ul>\nOur focus is smooth operational execution.\n<h3>Our strengths</h3>\nWe bridge strategy and execution:\n<ul>\n 	<li>Hands-on India setup experience</li>\n 	<li>Strong coordination across advisors</li>\n 	<li>Practical, implementable processes</li>\n 	<li>Alignment with HQ expectations</li>\n 	<li>Early risk identification</li>\n 	<li>Speed without compliance compromise</li>\n 	<li>Scalable operating frameworks</li>\n</ul>\nWe turn plans into functioning operations.\n<h2>Supply Chain &amp; Sourcing Advisory</h2>\nIndia offers significant opportunities for sourcing, manufacturing and supply-chain diversification—but success depends on rigorous partner selection and risk management. Our Supply Chain &amp; Sourcing Advisory services help clients design resilient, cost-effective and compliant supply chains aligned with global quality and ESG standards.\n\nWe support clients in evaluating suppliers, structuring sourcing models and mitigating risks related to quality, dependency, logistics and regulatory compliance. We also focus on "dual-sourcing" concepts and risk planning to ensure that your supply chain is resilient to local disruptions. Our work enables clients to build supply chains that are competitive, transparent and scalable.\n<h3>Our focus areas</h3>\nOur sourcing approach is structured:\n<ul>\n 	<li>Supplier identification and due diligence for quality, financial stability, and ethical standards</li>\n 	<li>Localization Roadmaps: Helping you transition sourcing from Europe to India in a phased, low-risk manner</li>\n 	<li>Cost and quality benchmarking</li>\n 	<li>Contracting and risk allocation</li>\n 	<li>Logistics and lead-time optimisation</li>\n 	<li>ESG and compliance assessments</li>\n 	<li>Dependency and concentration risk analysis</li>\n 	<li>Integration with global supply chains</li>\n</ul>\nOur focus is resilience and reliability.\n<h3>Our strengths</h3>\nWe protect continuity and quality:\n<ul>\n 	<li>Strong Indian supplier ecosystem access</li>\n 	<li>Commercial and compliance perspective</li>\n 	<li>Experience correcting failed sourcing models</li>\n 	<li>Risk-aware supplier selection</li>\n 	<li>Clear governance and monitoring</li>\n 	<li>Alignment with global standards</li>\n 	<li>Sustainable sourcing frameworks</li>\n</ul>\nWe help clients source with confidence.\n<h2>Sales Enablement &amp; Go-to-Market Support</h2>\nBuilding sales traction in India requires more than a strong product—it demands localised go-to-market strategies, pricing logic and sales governance. Our Sales Enablement &amp; Go-to-Market services help clients translate market opportunity into sustainable revenue.\n\nWe support clients in designing sales models, defining pricing strategies and enabling sales teams with the right tools, incentives and performance metrics. Our approach ensures that sales growth is scalable, compliant and aligned with headquarters’ expectations.\n<h3>Our focus areas</h3>\nOur work is commercially grounded:\n<ul>\n 	<li>Go-to-market and channel strategy - designing the initial strategy for launching your products or services in the Indian market</li>\n 	<li>Marketing Localisation: Adapting your global messaging and materials to resonate with Indian customer behavior</li>\n 	<li>Pricing and discount frameworks</li>\n 	<li>Sales organisation design</li>\n 	<li>Distributor and partner enablement</li>\n 	<li>Sales KPIs and incentive structures</li>\n 	<li>Pipeline and forecast discipline</li>\n 	<li>Performance diagnostics</li>\n</ul>\nOur focus is predictable revenue growth.\n<h3>Our strengths</h3>\nWe enable disciplined sales:\n\n- Strong understanding of Indian buying behaviour\n\n- Alignment with European governance norms\n\n- Practical sales-model experience\n\n- Clear pricing and margin logic\n\n- KPI-driven performance culture\n\n- Reduced channel conflict\n\n- Scalable sales frameworks\n\nWe help sales models perform - not just launch.', 'Operations, Supply Chain & Sourcing', 'Our India operations and supply chain advisory supports European companies with site selection, operational setup, sourcing, and go-to-market execution through practical, scalable, and risk-aware support for sustainable growth in India.', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '118-autosave-v1', '', '', '2026-03-11 14:19:41', '2026-03-11 13:19:41', '', 118, 'https://feboko.com/?p=178', 0, 'revision', '', 0),
	(179, 4, '2026-03-11 14:25:22', '2026-03-11 13:25:22', '<h2>HR Strategy</h2>\nBuilding a successful India operation requires an HR strategy that balances local realities with global standards. Our HR Strategy service supports organisations in designing people roadmaps that directly enable business growth, scalability, and long-term stability in India. We work closely with leadership teams to align organisational design, workforce planning, and HR policies with group-level frameworks while ensuring compliance with Indian labour laws and market practices.\n\nOur approach goes beyond policy design to focus on practical implementation—helping clients translate strategic intent into operational people processes. We address critical areas such as talent structure, leadership pipelines, performance expectations, and ESG-aligned people practices, ensuring that HR becomes a business enabler rather than an administrative function. The result is a clear, future-ready HR roadmap that supports growth ambitions in India while remaining fully aligned with European governance, culture, and risk standards.\n<h3>Our focus areas</h3>\nOur HR strategy work is grounded in linking people decisions directly to business outcomes, with emphasis on:\n<ul>\n 	<li>Organisational and workforce design aligned to growth plans</li>\n 	<li>HR policy architecture / Employee Handbook and localisation of global policies</li>\n 	<li>Talent and leadership pipeline planning</li>\n 	<li>Diversity, equity, and inclusion frameworks</li>\n 	<li>ESG-aligned people practices</li>\n 	<li>HR governance and decision-rights clarity</li>\n</ul>\nOur focus is on building HR structures that scale with the business and deliver measurable impact.\n<h3>Our strengths</h3>\nOur strength lies in combining strategic HR thinking with on-ground execution capability:\n<ul>\n 	<li>Strong understanding of European HR standards and expectations</li>\n 	<li>Practical, implementation-led approach</li>\n 	<li>Experience across growth, stabilisation, and turnaround phases</li>\n 	<li>Sensitivity to cultural and organisational dynamics</li>\n 	<li>Clear linkage between HR initiatives and business metrics</li>\n 	<li>Board-ready documentation and reporting</li>\n</ul>\nWe help clients move from HR intent to HR outcomes.\n<h2>HR Search</h2>\nHiring the right leadership and specialist talent is one of the most critical success factors for India operations. Our HR Search service delivers targeted executive and specialist search solutions with a strong emphasis on cultural fit, leadership maturity, and long-term retention. We support clients across senior management, functional leaders, and specialist roles, including C-suite positions such as CEOs and CFOs for Indian entities.\n\nOur search process is structured, discreet, and market-driven. We invest significant effort upfront in understanding role context, organisational culture, and stakeholder expectations. This ensures that shortlisted candidates are not only technically strong but also aligned with the client’s operating model, governance culture, and growth ambitions. By combining deep market mapping with rigorous assessment, we help clients build leadership teams that can operate confidently between European headquarters and Indian execution realities.\n<h3>Our focus areas</h3>\nOur search assignments are designed to ensure quality, fit, and sustainability:\n<ul>\n 	<li>Definition of role profiles and success criteria</li>\n 	<li>Market mapping and talent intelligence</li>\n 	<li>Assessment of leadership and cultural fit</li>\n 	<li>C-suite and senior leadership searches</li>\n 	<li>Offer structuring and negotiation support</li>\n 	<li>Onboarding and transition support</li>\n</ul>\nOur focus is on building leadership teams that endure beyond the initial hiring decision.\n<h3>Our strengths</h3>\nWe differentiate ourselves through credibility, discretion, and market insight:\n<ul>\n 	<li>Strong networks across key industrial clusters</li>\n 	<li>Transparent communication with clients and candidates</li>\n 	<li>Experience with expatriate and local leadership models</li>\n 	<li>High confidentiality and process discipline</li>\n 	<li>Long-term, relationship-driven approach</li>\n 	<li>Clear alignment with board and shareholder expectations</li>\n</ul>\nWe focus on leadership stability, not just placement.\n<h2>Employer of Record (EOR)</h2>\nOur Employer of Record (EOR) solutions enable organisations to deploy employees in India quickly and compliantly without establishing an immediate legal entity. This allows you to deploy personnel in India immediately, with us managing their payroll, contracts, and compliance. This "entity-lite" approach avoids "Permanent Establishment" (PE) risks while giving you the speed and flexibility to test the market before committing to a full-scale subsidiary. This model is particularly effective for early-stage market entry, pilot operations, or temporary project deployments.\n\nOur EOR framework is designed with governance and transition in mind. Clients retain operational control over employees, while we handle contractual, payroll, and compliance responsibilities in line with Indian labour and tax laws. Importantly, we structure EOR arrangements to allow a smooth transition to a fully owned Indian entity when business scale or strategy requires it. This ensures flexibility without compromising compliance or group-level governance standards.\n<h3>Our focus areas</h3>\nOur EOR offering focuses on compliant deployment with future flexibility:\n<ul>\n 	<li>Employment contracts and payroll administration</li>\n 	<li>Compliance with labour, tax, and social-security laws</li>\n 	<li>PE risk awareness and mitigation</li>\n 	<li>Ongoing employee lifecycle management</li>\n 	<li>Governance and reporting frameworks</li>\n 	<li>Transition planning to own entity</li>\n</ul>\nOur focus is on enabling speed while protecting long-term interests.\n<h3>Our strengths</h3>\nWe bring structure and risk discipline to EOR arrangements:\n<ul>\n 	<li>Strong governance and compliance frameworks</li>\n 	<li>Focus on reputational and regulatory protection</li>\n 	<li>Experience with European group expectations</li>\n 	<li>Clear exit and transition mechanisms</li>\n 	<li>Transparent reporting and documentation</li>\n 	<li>Business-friendly, risk-aware execution</li>\n</ul>\nWe enable market entry without locking clients into sub-optimal structures.\n<h2>Performance Evaluation &amp; Optimization</h2>\nPerformance management systems often fail in India when global frameworks are applied without localisation. Our Performance Evaluation &amp; Optimization service helps organisations design and implement performance systems that comply with Indian labour law while reflecting international standards and leadership expectations.\n\nWe work with management teams to define clear performance goals, appraisal processes, and reward mechanisms that drive accountability and execution. Beyond system design, we focus on diagnosing performance gaps and implementing corrective measures such as targeted training, role clarification, or incentive redesign. Our approach bridges the gap between expected and actual performance, ensuring that performance management becomes a practical tool for growth rather than a procedural exercise.\n<h3>Our focus areas</h3>\nOur work focuses on building performance systems that deliver results:\n<ul>\n 	<li>Goal-setting and KPI frameworks</li>\n 	<li>Appraisal and review processes</li>\n 	<li>Variable-pay and incentive design</li>\n 	<li>Feedback and performance dialogue culture</li>\n 	<li>Performance gap diagnostics</li>\n 	<li>Targeted optimisation interventions</li>\n</ul>\nOur emphasis is on performance improvement, not just evaluation.\n<h3>Our strengths</h3>\nWe combine structure with flexibility:\n<ul>\n 	<li>Proven templates suitable for mid-size entities</li>\n 	<li>Alignment with Indian labour regulations</li>\n 	<li>Integration with reward and development systems</li>\n 	<li>Practical, implementation-led mindset</li>\n 	<li>Sensitivity to cultural performance drivers</li>\n 	<li>Clear linkage to business outcomes</li>\n</ul>\nWe help turn performance frameworks into performance results.\n<h2>Inter Cultural Training</h2>\nCultural misalignment is one of the most underestimated risks in India-Europe collaboration. Our Inter-Cultural Training programmes prepare European and Indian teams to work together effectively by addressing real-world behavioural, communication, and decision-making differences.\n\nRather than theoretical models, our training focuses on practical business situations such as leadership styles, negotiation behaviour, feedback culture, and virtual collaboration. Programmes are tailored to project teams, leadership groups, or functional teams, enabling immediate application. The objective is to reduce friction, accelerate trust, and improve execution across borders.\n<h3>Our focus areas</h3>\nOur training programmes address real operational challenges:\n<ul>\n 	<li>Leadership and communication styles</li>\n 	<li>Decision-making and escalation patterns</li>\n 	<li>Negotiation behaviour</li>\n 	<li>Virtual and cross-border team collaboration</li>\n 	<li>India-specific business etiquette</li>\n 	<li>Managing expectations and misunderstandings</li>\n</ul>\nOur focus is on improving day-to-day collaboration.\n<h3>Our strengths</h3>\nOur trainers combine credibility with relevance:\n<ul>\n 	<li>Long-term experience in Europe and India</li>\n 	<li>Business-led, not academic approach</li>\n 	<li>High relevance for operational teams</li>\n 	<li>Customised, role-specific content</li>\n 	<li>Immediate applicability</li>\n 	<li>Strong feedback from participants</li>\n</ul>\nWe enable teams to work better together, faster.\n<h2>Risk Management and Transition Planning</h2>\nOperating a subsidiary in India involves unique organizational risks that can often go unnoticed by a European headquarters until they impact the bottom line. Our Risk Management and Transition Planning service is designed to provide a comprehensive audit of your local organizational health, focusing on structural integrity and long-term operational continuity. We identify potential risks within your organizational structure, such as over-centralized decision-making or unclear reporting lines that often cause friction between the Indian entity and the parent company. Simultaneously, we assess employee sentiment to identify dissatisfaction levels, helping to prevent high attrition and cultural misalignment—common challenges in the Indian talent market. Beyond the current state, we map future challenges, including regulatory shifts and talent scarcity, to ensure your business remains resilient. A critical component of our service is managing the transition of key leadership positions. Whether moving from an expatriate-led model to local management or preparing for a change in plant leadership, we ensure the preservation of corporate values and institutional knowledge throughout the handover process.\n<h3>Our focus areas</h3>\nOur risk work is structured and actionable:\n\n- Structural Risk Assessment: Evaluating reporting hierarchies and delegation of authority matrices to ensure they align with European governance standards while remaining agile enough for the Indian market.\n\n- Employee Sentiment &amp; Culture Mapping: Identifing "friction points" between European management styles and local employee expectations through structured interviews and surveys to reduce attrition and improve productivity.\n\n- Future Readiness &amp; Challenge Mapping: Conducting strategic analysis to anticipate upcoming hurdles in the Indian landscape, from labor market shifts to changing compliance requirements.\n\n- Leadership Succession Planning: Designing and overseeing structured handover protocols for MDs, CFOs, and Plant Heads to ensure a seamless transition without loss of operational momentum.\n\n- Organizational Conflict Mitigation: Identifying silos and internal power struggles that could hinder the implementation of the parent company\'s global strategy.\n\nOur focus is on resilience and preparedness.\n<h3>Our strengths</h3>\nWe combine European transparency with deep Indian psychological and market insights. Our team acts as an objective observer, bridging the communication gap between the German HQ and the local workforce. We specialize in sensitive change management, ensuring your corporate DNA is preserved during every leadership transition.', 'People & Governance', 'Our HR consulting India services support European companies with HR strategy, executive search, Employer of Record solutions, performance management, intercultural training, and governance-focused transition planning for scalable and compliant operations in India.', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '120-autosave-v1', '', '', '2026-03-11 14:25:22', '2026-03-11 13:25:22', '', 120, 'https://feboko.com/?p=179', 0, 'revision', '', 0),
	(180, 4, '2026-03-11 14:30:59', '2026-03-11 13:30:59', '<h2>Diagnostic Reviews</h2>\nOur Diagnostic Reviews provide "outside-in" view which is independent, structured health checks of Indian operations, designed to give shareholders and senior leadership a clear, fact-based view of performance, governance, and risk exposure. These reviews go beyond management reporting and surface-level audits, focusing on how the business actually functions on the ground. We examine financial controls, operational efficiency, governance practices, compliance posture, and alignment with group policies. Our work typically includes document reviews, data analysis, management interviews, and targeted site-level assessments. Where required, the scope can be expanded to special audits, forensic reviews, anti-corruption assessments, or financial due diligence in transactional or sensitive situations. Particular attention is paid to identifying root causes of underperformance, control breakdowns, or compliance gaps rather than isolated symptoms. The outcome is a concise, management-ready report that highlights key risks, prioritised issues, and actionable recommendations, enabling boards and executive teams to take informed decisions with clarity and confidence.\n<h3>Our focus areas</h3>\nOur diagnostic work is structured to deliver fast clarity while allowing deeper investigation where risks warrant it.\n<ul>\n 	<li>Financial, operational, and governance diagnostics</li>\n 	<li>Quick-scan assessments and deep-dive reviews</li>\n 	<li>Prioritised issue identification and action planning</li>\n 	<li>Special audits and forensic investigations</li>\n 	<li>Anti-corruption and integrity reviews</li>\n 	<li>Financial due diligence for transactions</li>\n</ul>\nThese focus areas ensure a balanced view across performance, compliance, and strategic risk.\n<h3>Our strengths</h3>\nOur strength lies in combining independence with practical insight into Indian business realities.\n<ul>\n 	<li>Neutral outside-in perspective</li>\n 	<li>Interdisciplinary teams across finance, operations, and governance</li>\n 	<li>Strong alignment with European board expectations</li>\n 	<li>Concise, decision-oriented reporting</li>\n 	<li>Actionable recommendations, not theoretical findings</li>\n</ul>\nThis allows management to move from diagnosis to decision swiftly and confidently.\n<h2>Interim Management</h2>\nOur Interim Management services support organisations during periods of transition, disruption, or accelerated change in India. We deploy experienced interim leaders (with a back office team for specialized areas) who step into senior roles with full operational responsibility, ensuring continuity while driving clearly defined outcomes. Typical situations include leadership transitions, crisis stabilisation, post-acquisition integration, restructuring phases, or preparation for exit. Our interim managers bring both India operating experience and a strong understanding of multinational governance expectations. They work closely with local teams while maintaining transparent reporting to headquarters and boards. Each assignment is defined by a clear mandate, performance metrics, and timelines, ensuring accountability and measurable progress. Beyond stabilisation, interim leaders often lay the groundwork for long-term improvements by strengthening processes, controls, and leadership capability. The objective is not merely to “fill a gap” but to create tangible value and leave the organisation stronger at the end of the assignment.\n<h3>Our focus areas</h3>\nOur interim engagements are structured around clear authority, accountability, and outcomes.\n<ul>\n 	<li>Interim CXO and senior leadership roles</li>\n 	<li>Project and transformation leadership</li>\n 	<li>Crisis and turnaround management</li>\n 	<li>Operational stabilisation and execution</li>\n 	<li>Transition and succession support</li>\n</ul>\nThese focus areas ensure rapid impact without disrupting governance structures.\n<h3>Our strengths</h3>\nOur interim capability combines speed, credibility, and execution discipline.\n<ul>\n 	<li>Curated network of India-experienced leaders</li>\n 	<li>Rapid mobilisation and onboarding</li>\n 	<li>Clear mandates aligned with board objectives</li>\n 	<li>Strong governance and reporting discipline</li>\n 	<li>Hands-on, execution-driven leadership</li>\n</ul>\nThis enables organisations to navigate critical phases with control and confidence.\n<h2>Restructuring</h2>\nOur Restructuring services support European and global groups in addressing operational and financial challenges within Indian subsidiaries and joint ventures. We work across the full restructuring lifecycle, from early diagnostics and scenario planning to on-ground implementation. Our approach reflects the complexities of Indian labour laws, regulatory constraints, stakeholder sensitivities, and reputational risks. We help design turnaround strategies that balance cost optimisation with business continuity, covering footprint rationalisation, organisational restructuring, process redesign, and financial realignment. Stakeholder management is a central component of our work, including engagement with partners, employees, lenders, and regulators. Where required, we coordinate closely with legal, tax, and financial advisors to ensure consistency and compliance. The objective is to stabilise operations, restore performance, and protect group interests while building a sustainable operating model for the future.\n<h3>Our focus areas</h3>\nOur restructuring work is anchored in practicality and disciplined execution.\n<ul>\n 	<li>Turnaround and recovery planning</li>\n 	<li>Cost and footprint optimisation</li>\n 	<li>Organisational and process restructuring</li>\n 	<li>Stakeholder negotiations and alignment</li>\n 	<li>Communication and change management</li>\n</ul>\nThese focus areas ensure restructuring efforts deliver lasting impact rather than short-term fixes.\n<h3>Our strengths</h3>\nOur strength lies in combining restructuring expertise with local execution capability.\n<ul>\n 	<li>Proven restructuring know-how</li>\n 	<li>Deep understanding of Indian operating realities</li>\n 	<li>Strong focus on continuity and risk mitigation</li>\n 	<li>Reputation-conscious approach</li>\n 	<li>Hands-on implementation support</li>\n</ul>\nThis allows clients to navigate restructuring with control and credibility.\n<h2>Conflict Resolution / Dispute Resolution</h2>\nOur Conflict Resolution services help organisations resolve sensitive disputes in India before they escalate into litigation, arbitration, or long-term relationship damage. We act as independent advisors and facilitators in conflicts involving shareholders, joint-venture partners, customers, or senior employees. Our approach blends structured mediation techniques with a deep understanding of cultural dynamics, governance expectations, and commercial realities. We support clients in clarifying issues, assessing risks, defining negotiation strategies, and managing stakeholder communication. Where disputes intersect with legal proceedings, including arbitration, we work alongside legal counsel to ensure business considerations are fully addressed. Confidentiality, balance, and long-term value preservation are central to our methodology. The goal is not only dispute resolution but the protection of business continuity and trust.\n<h3>Our focus areas</h3>\nOur conflict resolution approach is designed to de-escalate risk while protecting relationships.\n<ul>\n 	<li>Mediation frameworks and facilitation</li>\n 	<li>Negotiation strategy development</li>\n 	<li>Risk and scenario analysis</li>\n 	<li>Stakeholder coordination</li>\n 	<li>Arbitration support (non-legal)</li>\n</ul>\nThese focus areas help resolve disputes constructively and efficiently.\n<h3>Our strengths</h3>\nOur strength lies in navigating sensitive situations with cultural and commercial awareness.\n<ul>\n 	<li>Culturally sensitive facilitation</li>\n 	<li>Balance between European governance and Indian realities</li>\n 	<li>Strong emphasis on relationship preservation</li>\n 	<li>Discreet and confidential handling</li>\n 	<li>Business-first problem-solving approach</li>\n</ul>\nThis enables durable outcomes even in complex disputes.\n<h2>Exit Management</h2>\nOur Exit Management services provide structured support for organisations scaling down, exiting India, or reshaping their geographic footprint within the country. Exits in India involve complex regulatory, labour, tax, and reputational considerations that require careful planning and disciplined execution. We support clients from strategic evaluation through final completion, covering options such as sale, carve-out, closure, or liquidation. Our work includes planning for employee transitions, asset disposal, contractual settlements, and statutory clearances, as well as designing communication strategies for key stakeholders. Particular emphasis is placed on safeguarding the interests of shareholders and directors and ensuring compliance with Indian law. Our structured approach reduces uncertainty, mitigates risk, and ensures an orderly and defensible exit process.\n<h3>Our focus areas</h3>\nOur exit support is designed to protect value while ensuring regulatory compliance.\n<ul>\n 	<li>Exit option evaluation and scenario planning</li>\n 	<li>Employee and asset transition management</li>\n 	<li>Regulatory approvals ("no-objection certificates") and clearances</li>\n 	<li>Stakeholder and communication strategies</li>\n 	<li>Company closure, liquidation, winding-up, strike-off</li>\n 	<li>Ensuring brand or company name availability for potential re-entry</li>\n</ul>\nThese focus areas ensure clarity and control throughout the exit process.\n<h3>Our strengths</h3>\nOur strength lies in executing exits with precision and reputational care.\n<ul>\n 	<li>Experience across exits and turnarounds</li>\n 	<li>Strong governance and compliance focus</li>\n 	<li>Close coordination with legal and tax advisors</li>\n 	<li>Clear, step-by-step execution roadmap</li>\n 	<li>Controlled delivery from decision to completion</li>\n</ul>\nThis enables boards to exit with confidence and minimal residual risk.', 'Turnaround, Crisis & Interim Management', 'Our India business transformation advisory supports European companies with diagnostic reviews, interim management, restructuring, dispute resolution, and exit management through independent, execution-focused, and governance-aligned support for Indian operations.', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '122-autosave-v1', '', '', '2026-03-11 14:30:59', '2026-03-11 13:30:59', '', 122, 'https://feboko.com/?p=180', 0, 'revision', '', 0),
	(181, 4, '2026-03-11 15:12:56', '2026-03-11 14:12:56', '<h2>M&amp;A Advisory</h2>\nOur M&amp;A Advisory services support European and global companies across the full transaction lifecycle involving Indian targets or assets. We advise on both buy-side and sell-side transactions, combining strategic insight with rigorous execution support. Our role typically begins at the opportunity identification stage, supporting target search and strategic screening, and extends through due diligence coordination, valuation input, transaction structuring, and SPA negotiations. We work as an integrated interface between investors, Indian counterparties, advisors, and internal stakeholders, ensuring alignment across commercial, legal, tax, and financial dimensions. Particular attention is paid to India-specific risks, regulatory considerations, governance expectations, and post-transaction integration challenges. Beyond signing and closing, we support clients with post-merger planning to ensure operational continuity and value realisation. Our approach is pragmatic, transparent, and aligned with European investment committee expectations, enabling decision-makers to navigate complex cross-border transactions with confidence.\n<h3>Our focus areas</h3>\nOur M&amp;A advisory approach is designed to provide end-to-end transaction clarity and control.\n<ul>\n 	<li>Target identification and strategic screening</li>\n 	<li>Coordination of commercial, legal, tax, and financial due diligence</li>\n 	<li>Valuation inputs and deal-economics analysis</li>\n 	<li>SPA and transaction documentation support</li>\n 	<li>Regulatory and closing coordination</li>\n 	<li>Post-merger integration planning</li>\n</ul>\nThese focus areas ensure transactions are not only completed but successfully embedded into the group.\n<h3>Our strengths</h3>\nOur strength lies in acting as a single, accountable advisor across workstreams.\n<ul>\n 	<li>Deep cross-border M&amp;A experience with European investors</li>\n 	<li>Strong coordination across legal, tax, and finance advisors</li>\n 	<li>Clear communication with boards and investment committees</li>\n 	<li>Strong understanding of Indian deal dynamics</li>\n 	<li>Execution discipline from origination to integration</li>\n</ul>\nThis enables smoother transactions and better investment outcomes.\n<h2>Corporate Law M&amp;A</h2>\nOur Corporate Law M&amp;A services focus on the legal execution of mergers, acquisitions, restructurings, and reorganisations involving Indian entities. We support clients through all legal stages of the transaction, from structuring and documentation to regulatory approvals and post-closing implementation. Our team is experienced in drafting and negotiating SPAs, share subscription agreements, shareholders’ agreements, and related ancillary documents in line with international deal standards. We work closely with European counsel to ensure consistency with group-level transaction frameworks while addressing India-specific legal and regulatory requirements. Post-closing, we assist with corporate reorganisations, governance updates, and statutory filings to ensure seamless integration. Our approach balances technical precision with commercial practicality, enabling transactions to progress efficiently while protecting client interests.\n<h3>Our focus areas</h3>\nOur legal support is structured to ensure certainty, compliance, and execution efficiency.\n<ul>\n 	<li>Transaction structuring and legal architecture</li>\n 	<li>Drafting and negotiation of SPAs and ancillary agreements</li>\n 	<li>Regulatory approvals and statutory filings</li>\n 	<li>Closing coordination and implementation</li>\n 	<li>Post-closing reorganisations and clean-ups</li>\n</ul>\nThese focus areas ensure legal robustness across the transaction lifecycle.\n<h3>Our strengths</h3>\nOur legal capability combines international standards with Indian execution expertise.\n<ul>\n 	<li>Lawyers experienced in cross-border M&amp;A transactions</li>\n 	<li>Familiarity with European deal documentation practices</li>\n 	<li>Efficient collaboration with European legal teams</li>\n 	<li>Clear, precise drafting in English</li>\n 	<li>Strong focus on timelines and execution certainty</li>\n</ul>\nThis ensures legally sound and commercially aligned transactions.\n<h2>Taxation M&amp;A</h2>\nOur Taxation M&amp;A services provide comprehensive tax support for acquisitions, divestments, and group reorganisations involving India. We assist clients in identifying tax risks and opportunities at an early stage and designing tax-efficient acquisition and financing structures that align with commercial objectives and regulatory requirements. Our work includes detailed tax due diligence, assessment of historic exposures, and evaluation of transaction structuring alternatives. We also support the design of step-plans and post-deal tax integration, ensuring that intended structures are practically implementable and sustainable. Close coordination with corporate, legal, and finance teams ensures that tax considerations are embedded into transaction decision-making rather than treated as an afterthought. Our advice is grounded in current Indian tax law, treaty interpretation, and administrative practice, with a strong focus on clarity and defensibility.\n<h3>Our focus areas</h3>\nOur tax advisory is designed to support informed transaction decisions and smooth integration.\n<ul>\n 	<li>Tax due diligence and risk assessment</li>\n 	<li>Acquisition and financing structuring</li>\n 	<li>Step-plan and reorganisation design</li>\n 	<li>Cross-border tax considerations</li>\n 	<li>Post-deal tax integration and alignment</li>\n</ul>\nThese focus areas ensure tax efficiency without compromising compliance.\n<h3>Our strengths</h3>\nOur strength lies in translating complex tax issues into clear business decisions.\n<ul>\n 	<li>Close integration with corporate and finance teams</li>\n 	<li>Clear articulation of risks and opportunities</li>\n 	<li>Practical, implementation-oriented advice</li>\n 	<li>Strong understanding of Indian tax administration</li>\n 	<li>Continued support beyond transaction closing</li>\n</ul>\nThis enables sustainable and defensible tax outcomes.\n<h2>Business Valuations</h2>\nOur Business Valuation services provide independent, objective valuations for transactions, financial reporting, restructuring exercises, and shareholder matters involving Indian businesses. We support clients across a wide range of valuation contexts, including acquisitions, divestments, impairment testing, purchase price allocation, and fairness assessments. Our valuations are grounded in recognised international standards and tailored to the expectations of auditors, group controllers, and investment committees. We combine rigorous financial analysis with a deep understanding of India-specific market dynamics, regulatory factors, and risk profiles. Our models are transparent, well-documented, and designed to withstand scrutiny from auditors and stakeholders. The outcome is a defensible valuation that supports sound decision-making and governance.\n<h3>Our focus areas</h3>\nOur valuation work is designed to support transactions and governance requirements.\n<ul>\n 	<li>Equity and enterprise valuations</li>\n 	<li>Transaction and deal-support valuations</li>\n 	<li>Purchase price allocation inputs</li>\n 	<li>Impairment testing support</li>\n 	<li>Fairness and shareholder assessments</li>\n</ul>\nThese focus areas ensure valuations are robust, transparent, and decision-useful.\n<h3>Our strengths</h3>\nOur valuation capability combines technical rigour with stakeholder awareness.\n<ul>\n 	<li>Use of recognised valuation methodologies</li>\n 	<li>Familiarity with audit and group reporting expectations</li>\n 	<li>Transparent, review-friendly models</li>\n 	<li>Clear assumptions and documentation</li>\n 	<li>Independent and objective perspective</li>\n</ul>\nThis ensures credibility with all transaction stakeholders.\n<h2>Financial Modelling</h2>\nOur Financial Modelling services support investment decisions, strategic planning, and scenario analysis for India-related projects and transactions. We develop robust, flexible models that reflect the commercial, regulatory, and operational realities of operating in India. Our models are used for investment cases, business planning, funding assessments, and stress testing under multiple scenarios. Particular emphasis is placed on clarity of assumptions, logical structure, and auditability, ensuring models can be reviewed and used confidently by group finance teams and investment committees. We also support sensitivity analysis and funding-structure simulations to help management understand risk exposures and return drivers. Each model is delivered with clear documentation and handover support to enable ongoing internal use.\n<h3>Our focus areas</h3>\nOur modelling work is designed to support decision-making under uncertainty.\n<ul>\n 	<li>Project and business-plan models</li>\n 	<li>Integrated financial projections</li>\n 	<li>Sensitivity and scenario analysis</li>\n 	<li>Funding and capital-structure simulations</li>\n 	<li>Model review and refinement</li>\n</ul>\nThese focus areas ensure models remain practical and decision-oriented.\n<h3>Our strengths</h3>\nOur modelling strength lies in combining analytical depth with usability.\n<ul>\n 	<li>Modellers with consulting and industry backgrounds</li>\n 	<li>Strong understanding of investor and board requirements</li>\n 	<li>Clear structure and transparent assumptions</li>\n 	<li>Detailed documentation and handover</li>\n 	<li>Models designed for ongoing internal use</li>\n</ul>\nThis enables finance teams to rely on models beyond the transaction phase.', 'Mergers & Acquisitions', 'Our India M&A advisory supports European and global companies across acquisitions, divestments, valuations, tax structuring, legal execution, and financial modelling with pragmatic, cross-border aligned support throughout the full transaction lifecycle.', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '126-autosave-v1', '', '', '2026-03-11 15:12:56', '2026-03-11 14:12:56', '', 126, 'https://feboko.com/?p=181', 0, 'revision', '', 0),
	(182, 4, '2026-03-11 15:18:59', '2026-03-11 14:18:59', '<h2>Special Valuation Branch Assessments</h2>\nOur SVB Assessment services provide comprehensive advisory and documentation support for customs matters involving related-party imports into India. We assist clients in managing SVB investigations by analysing intercompany relationships, pricing mechanisms, and contractual arrangements to establish arm’s-length compliance under Indian customs law. Our support includes preparation of detailed submissions, responses to authority queries, and guidance on procedural requirements such as PD bonds, zero loading, and provisional assessments. We also advise on aligning intercompany agreements, royalty structures, and management fee arrangements to reduce future exposure. By integrating customs, transfer pricing, and legal perspectives, we help clients achieve clarity, closure, and predictability in complex SVB proceedings.\n<h3>Our focus areas</h3>\nOur SVB approach is designed to achieve defensible and sustainable outcomes.\n<ul>\n 	<li>Relationship and pricing analysis</li>\n 	<li>Balancing the legally mandatory provisions of Transfer Prices under Direct Tax and Customs Regimes</li>\n 	<li>Preparation of SVB submissions and documentation (including Annexure A and Annexure B)</li>\n 	<li>PD bond and provisional assessment support</li>\n 	<li>Royalty and management-fee evaluations</li>\n 	<li>Authority interactions and proactive query management with an objective of zero loading</li>\n 	<li>Process and documentation adjustments</li>\n</ul>\nThese focus areas reduce uncertainty and future customs exposure.\n<h3>Our strengths</h3>\nOur strength is the integration of multiple disciplines into one solution.\n<ul>\n 	<li>Combined customs, transfer-pricing and legal expertise</li>\n 	<li>Strong experience with European group structures</li>\n 	<li>Ability to manage complex SVB reviews</li>\n 	<li>Clear, well-structured documentation</li>\n 	<li>Practical resolution-oriented mindset</li>\n</ul>\nThis ensures efficient closure and long-term compliance.\n<h2>Advisory Board</h2>\nOur Advisory Board services support Indian subsidiaries and joint ventures by providing independent, experienced guidance aligned with group governance expectations. We assist in designing advisory boards, defining their mandate, and participating as independent advisers where appropriate. Our role typically includes strategic sparring with management, review of operational performance, and alignment of local decisions with group priorities. Advisory boards are particularly effective in bridging cultural, governance, and execution gaps between European headquarters and Indian management teams. Our advisers bring hands-on experience across India and Europe, ensuring discussions remain practical, commercially grounded, and forward-looking. The objective is to strengthen decision-making, governance discipline, and leadership effectiveness without creating additional statutory complexity.\n<h3>Our focus areas</h3>\nOur advisory board engagement focuses on value-adding governance.\n<ul>\n 	<li>Board composition and role definition</li>\n 	<li>Charters, agendas and operating frameworks</li>\n 	<li>Strategic and operational sparring</li>\n 	<li>Management performance review</li>\n 	<li>Alignment with group governance expectations</li>\n 	<li>These focus areas enhance oversight while supporting management autonomy.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Our strengths</h3>\nOur advisory capability is built on experience and independence.\n<ul>\n 	<li>Senior advisers with India and Europe exposure</li>\n 	<li>Objective, non-executive perspective</li>\n 	<li>Strong understanding of Mittelstand governance culture</li>\n 	<li>Hands-on, solution-oriented input</li>\n 	<li>Trusted interface between HQ and local management</li>\n</ul>\nThis strengthens governance without slowing execution.\n<h2>Dispute Resolution</h2>\nOur Dispute Resolution services support clients in managing, resolving, and mitigating commercial, regulatory, and tax disputes in India with a strong focus on business continuity and value preservation. We work closely with management teams to assess the nature and severity of disputes at an early stage, helping clients understand legal exposure, financial implications, and potential reputational risks. Our approach emphasises pragmatic evaluation of litigation and settlement options, enabling informed decision-making before disputes escalate into prolonged and costly proceedings.\n\nWe assist in developing negotiation and settlement strategies that balance legal position with commercial realities, often helping clients achieve faster and more cost-effective outcomes. Where specialist legal counsel is required, we coordinate closely with external advisors to ensure a consistent strategy, clear communication, and efficient information flow. Our role extends to supporting documentation, position papers, and internal alignment across finance, tax, and operational teams.\n\nWhere disputes proceed to formal litigation or arbitration, we provide structured support in strategy development, evidence preparation, and ongoing coordination, ensuring clarity and control throughout the process. By combining legal understanding with commercial insight and cultural sensitivity, we help clients protect their interests while minimising disruption to their Indian operations and long-term business objectives.\n<h3>Our focus areas</h3>\nOur dispute support prioritises resolution over escalation.\n<ul>\n 	<li>Litigation risk assessment</li>\n 	<li>Strategy and settlement planning</li>\n 	<li>Negotiation and mediation support</li>\n 	<li>Coordination with legal counsel</li>\n 	<li>Documentation and stakeholder communication</li>\n</ul>\nThese focus areas help manage disputes pragmatically and efficiently.\n<h3>Our strengths</h3>\nOur strength lies in balancing firmness with relationship preservation.\n<ul>\n 	<li>Culturally sensitive dispute handling</li>\n 	<li>Multi-disciplinary view on legal, financial and reputational risk</li>\n 	<li>Experience with European governance expectations</li>\n 	<li>Focus on commercial outcomes</li>\n 	<li>Clear communication with management and boards</li>\n</ul>\nThis protects long-term business interests.\n<h2>Compliance &amp; Risk Management Audit</h2>\nOur Compliance &amp; Risk Management Audit services deliver independent and objective assessments of an Indian entity’s compliance framework, internal control environment, and overall risk-management processes. We evaluate how effectively local policies, procedures, and controls align with Indian regulatory requirements, group governance standards, and relevant international best practices. Our reviews go beyond checklist-based compliance to examine how controls operate in practice and how risks are identified, monitored, and managed across the organisation.\n\nThrough structured policy reviews, control testing, and stakeholder discussions, we identify compliance gaps, control weaknesses, and emerging risk areas. Each finding is assessed in terms of its financial, operational, regulatory, and reputational impact, allowing management to prioritise remediation efforts effectively. Our recommendations are practical, proportionate, and supported by a clear and actionable implementation roadmap, ensuring that improvements can be embedded into day-to-day operations.\n\nThe objective of our audits is not only to highlight deficiencies but to strengthen governance, accountability, and risk awareness at all organisational levels. Our reporting is concise, clearly structured, and tailored for senior management, audit committees, and group oversight functions, enabling informed decision-making and sustained improvement in the control environment.\n<h3>Our focus areas</h3>\nOur audits are designed to strengthen control environments.\n<ul>\n 	<li>Policy and control framework reviews</li>\n 	<li>Regulatory compliance assessments</li>\n 	<li>Risk identification and prioritisation</li>\n 	<li>Remediation recommendations</li>\n 	<li>Implementation roadmaps</li>\n</ul>\nThese focus areas enhance transparency and control maturity.\n<h3>Our strengths</h3>\nOur strength lies in combining audit rigour with advisory insight.\n<ul>\n 	<li>Audit and advisory teams working together</li>\n 	<li>Practical, implementable recommendations</li>\n 	<li>Clear reporting for audit committees</li>\n 	<li>Alignment with group risk frameworks</li>\n 	<li>Business-focused approach</li>\n</ul>\nThis ensures audits drive improvement, not just compliance.\n<h2>Internal Audits</h2>\nOur Internal Audit services deliver risk-based, independent assurance tailored to both group governance standards and the operational realities of doing business in India. We assess key business processes, internal controls, and fraud-risk exposures across functions, locations, and legal entities, with a clear focus on areas that matter most to management and group oversight bodies. Our audits are designed to provide insight, not disruption, and to support stronger decision-making rather than merely identifying non-compliance.\n\nOur methodology is aligned with international internal-audit standards and best practices, while remaining pragmatic, proportionate, and business-oriented. Through process walkthroughs, control testing, data analysis, and targeted interviews, we identify control gaps, inefficiencies, and root causes of recurring issues. Particular attention is given to fraud-risk indicators, segregation of duties, and the effectiveness of management oversight.\n\nEach audit concludes with clear, prioritised findings and practical recommendations that are realistic to implement within the Indian operating environment. We support management through structured remediation plans and follow-up tracking to ensure agreed actions are executed and sustained. Our reporting is concise, structured, and suitable for senior management and audit committees, providing transparency, accountability, and continuous improvement across the organisation.\n<h3>Our focus areas</h3>\nOur internal audits focus on risk and value protection.\n<ul>\n 	<li>Process and control testing</li>\n 	<li>Fraud-risk assessments</li>\n 	<li>Operational and compliance reviews</li>\n 	<li>Follow-up and remediation tracking</li>\n 	<li>Alignment with group audit plans</li>\n</ul>\nThese focus areas strengthen internal control effectiveness.\n<h3>Our strengths</h3>\nOur audit approach is constructive and solution-driven.\n<ul>\n 	<li>Alignment with international audit standards</li>\n 	<li>Multilingual, cross-functional teams</li>\n 	<li>Strong understanding of Indian operations</li>\n 	<li>Practical recommendations</li>\n 	<li>Collaborative engagement style</li>\n</ul>\nThis ensures audits are effective and well-received.\n<h2>Financial Due Diligence</h2>\nOur Financial Due Diligence services support investors, acquirers, and lenders in evaluating Indian businesses across acquisitions, divestments, joint ventures, and strategic investments. We go beyond headline numbers to assess the sustainability and quality of earnings, working-capital dynamics, cash-flow generation, and underlying business drivers. Our reviews identify accounting risks, one-off items, related-party exposures, and areas requiring post-transaction adjustments. We place strong emphasis on understanding local accounting practices and reconciling them with international reporting expectations, ensuring that findings are decision-relevant for European boards and investment committees. Our due diligence outputs are concise, analytical, and clearly prioritised, enabling clients to assess valuation assumptions, negotiate transaction terms, and plan post-deal integration with confidence. The objective is to provide a clear financial picture that supports informed decision-making while avoiding unnecessary complexity.\n<h3>Our focus areas</h3>\nOur financial due diligence is designed to deliver clarity and deal certainty.\n<ul>\n 	<li>Quality of earnings and normalised EBITDA analysis</li>\n 	<li>Working-capital and cash-flow assessments</li>\n 	<li>Identification and reporting of ongoing tax defaults, litigations and pending demands</li>\n 	<li>Accounting policy and financial-reporting review</li>\n 	<li>Identification of one-off items and adjustments</li>\n 	<li>Related-party transaction analysis</li>\n 	<li>Debt, contingencies and off-balance-sheet exposures</li>\n</ul>\nThese focus areas ensure a robust understanding of financial performance and risk.\n<h3>Our strengths</h3>\nOur strength lies in combining analytical depth with decision relevance.\n<ul>\n 	<li>Strong experience in Indian mid-market transactions</li>\n 	<li>Alignment with European reporting and governance standards</li>\n 	<li>Clear, board-ready reporting</li>\n 	<li>Focus on value drivers and deal implications</li>\n 	<li>Practical support during negotiations and closing</li>\n</ul>\nThis enables confident valuation, pricing and integration decisions.\n<h2>Forensic Audits</h2>\nOur Forensic Audit services support organisations in identifying, investigating, and responding to suspected fraud, misconduct, financial irregularities, and governance failures within Indian operations. We conduct independent, confidential investigations using structured methodologies that preserve evidence integrity and withstand regulatory or legal scrutiny. Our work typically includes transaction analysis, data review, document examination, and management interviews. We also assist clients in understanding root causes, control weaknesses, and behavioural risks that may have enabled the issue. Our forensic engagements are handled with discretion and cultural sensitivity, recognising the reputational, legal, and operational implications involved. In addition to investigation outcomes, we provide clear recommendations to strengthen controls, improve oversight, and prevent recurrence. The objective is not only to establish facts, but to restore trust and strengthen governance frameworks.\n<h3>Our focus areas</h3>\nOur forensic work focuses on fact-finding and risk containment.\n<ul>\n 	<li>Fraud and misconduct investigations looking for specific evidence or indications of financial manipulation</li>\n 	<li>Financial irregularity and leakage analysis with focus on finding and recovering funds that have been misappropriated</li>\n 	<li>Review of internal controls and governance failures</li>\n 	<li>Evidence preservation and documentation</li>\n 	<li>Management interviews and reporting</li>\n 	<li>Remediation and preventive control design</li>\n</ul>\nThese focus areas support credible investigations and long-term risk mitigation.\n<h3>Our strengths</h3>\nOur strength lies in independence, rigour, and discretion.\n<ul>\n 	<li>Experienced forensic and investigation professionals</li>\n 	<li>Structured, defensible investigation methodologies</li>\n 	<li>High confidentiality and sensitivity handling</li>\n 	<li>Clear, factual and unbiased reporting</li>\n 	<li>Practical recommendations to strengthen controls</li>\n</ul>\nThis ensures credible outcomes and improved organisational resilience.\n<h2>Anti Corruption Audits</h2>\nOur Anti-Corruption Audit services provide focused and independent assessments of bribery and corruption risks within Indian operations and extended third-party networks. We review policies, internal controls, and day-to-day practices against applicable Indian regulations as well as European and US anti-corruption standards. Our work includes targeted third-party due diligence, transaction and payment testing, and evaluation of training, reporting, and monitoring mechanisms. The objective is to identify vulnerabilities at an early stage and address them before they escalate into regulatory or reputational issues. We place particular emphasis on translating global compliance requirements into practical, workable local procedures that can be embedded into routine business operations without disrupting commercial effectiveness.\n<h3>Our focus areas</h3>\nOur reviews focus on prevention and accountability.\n<ul>\n 	<li>Looking for specific evidence or indications of bribe, kickbacks and manipulation\n- Policy and control assessments</li>\n 	<li>Third-party risk reviews</li>\n 	<li>Transaction testing</li>\n 	<li>Training and awareness evaluation</li>\n 	<li>Monitoring and remediation measures</li>\n</ul>\nThese focus areas reduce regulatory and reputational risk.\n<h3>Our strengths</h3>\nOur strength is translating global standards into local practice.\n<ul>\n 	<li>Awareness of EU and US anti-corruption regimes</li>\n 	<li>Strong understanding of Indian enforcement realities</li>\n 	<li>Practical, implementable recommendations</li>\n 	<li>Clear documentation</li>\n 	<li>Preventive risk mindset</li>\n</ul>\nThis strengthens compliance culture sustainably.\n<h2>SAP &amp; IT Solutions</h2>\nOur SAP &amp; IT Solutions services support the implementation, localisation, and optimisation of ERP and IT systems that integrate Indian entities seamlessly into global platforms. We assist with system rollouts, tax and regulatory localisation, process automation, and the design of robust access and security frameworks. Our approach balances global template adherence with the practical requirements of operating in India, ensuring accurate reporting, strong internal controls, and audit readiness. By combining process, tax, and IT expertise, we help clients achieve stable, compliant, and scalable system environments that support efficient operations while remaining fully aligned with group IT architecture and governance standards.\n<h3>Our focus areas</h3>\nOur IT support focuses on integration and reliability.\n<ul>\n 	<li>SAP and ERP rollouts</li>\n 	<li>Localisation of Chart of Accounts</li>\n 	<li>Process automation</li>\n 	<li>Access and security concepts</li>\n 	<li>Integration with global templates</li>\n</ul>\nThese focus areas ensure system effectiveness and consistency.\n<h3>Our strengths</h3>\nOur strength lies in bridging IT and compliance.\n<ul>\n 	<li>Combined process, tax and IT expertise</li>\n 	<li>Experience with global ERP integrations</li>\n 	<li>- Strong focus on controls and reporting</li>\n 	<li>- Practical implementation support</li>\n 	<li>- Clear coordination with group IT teams</li>\n</ul>\nThis ensures stable and compliant system environments.\n<h2>Transaction Advisory</h2>\nManaging the commercial interactions between a European parent company and its Indian subsidiary requires a delicate balance of operational efficiency and strict regulatory adherence. Our Transaction Advisory service specializes in structuring cross-border operating transactions—ranging from the supply of raw materials and machinery to the provision of high-value technical services and management support. We focus on creating robust frameworks that prevent the accidental creation of a "Permanent Establishment" (PE) in India, a common trap that can lead to significant unintended tax liabilities for the overseas entity. Our advisory encompasses a 360-degree view, ensuring that intercompany agreements are fully compliant with India’s Foreign Exchange Management Act (FEMA) while remaining optimized from both a direct tax (Withholding/DTAA) and indirect tax (GST) perspective. By engineering the transaction flow correctly from the outset, we help European firms minimize tax leakages and regulatory friction. This strategic approach ensures that your operational model is not only commercially viable but also resilient against the aggressive scrutiny of Indian tax authorities, facilitating seamless profit repatriation and transparent group-level financial reporting.\n<h3>Our focus areas</h3>\nOur transaction support focuses on informed decision-making and on:\nOperating Model Structuring: Designing the flow of goods and services between the HQ and the Indian entity to maximize operational speed while minimizing tax nexus risks.\n\nPermanent Establishment (PE) Mitigation: Conducting rigorous reviews of "Secondment Agreements" and "Service Level Agreements" to protect the European parent from unintended Indian tax exposure.\n\nDirect Tax &amp; DTAA Optimization: Leveraging Double Taxation Avoidance Agreements (DTAA) to optimize withholding tax rates on royalties, dividends, and fees for technical services.\n\nIndirect Tax (GST) Strategy: Structuring import-export transactions to ensure GST compliance and maximize the recovery of Input Tax Credits (ITC), preventing "tax-on-tax" costs.\n\nFEMA &amp; Regulatory Compliance: Ensuring all cross-border payments and capital flows meet the stringent requirements of the Reserve Bank of India, avoiding compounding penalties.\n\nIntercompany Agreement Drafting: Crafting bespoke commercial contracts that are legally enforceable in India and compliant with international transfer pricing standards.\n<h3>Our strengths</h3>\nWe combine technical legal expertise with deep tax specialization, offering a "one-stop" solution for cross-border engineering. Our team excels at translating complex Indian FEMA and tax codes into actionable strategies that align with European group policies, ensuring audit-proof structures for your international operations.\n<h2>Workshops &amp; Trainings</h2>\nOur Workshops are tailored learning sessions designed to equip management and project teams with practical knowledge on India-related legal, tax, cultural, and operational topics. The sessions combine structured insights with real project experience, supporting both market-entry readiness and the effective management of ongoing Indian operations. We focus on practical implications rather than theory, enabling participants to translate learning directly into action. Workshop formats are interactive and adapted to client-specific objectives, seniority levels, and functional needs. All materials are designed for reuse in internal training programmes, helping organisations build lasting in-house capability and alignment across teams working with India.\n<h3>Our focus areas</h3>\nOur workshops are designed for immediate applicability.\n<ul>\n 	<li>- Market-entry readiness</li>\n 	<li>- Compliance and governance awareness</li>\n 	<li>- Finance and controlling in India</li>\n 	<li>- Cultural and operational best practices</li>\n 	<li>- Peer learning from European investors</li>\n</ul>\nThese focus areas support informed and confident teams.\n<h3>Our strengths</h3>\nOur strength lies in practitioner-led learning.\n<ul>\n 	<li>- Trainers with real project experience</li>\n 	<li>- Interactive, discussion-based formats</li>\n 	<li>- Practical, reusable materials</li>\n 	<li>- Strong relevance to European teams</li>\n 	<li>- Focus on real business scenarios</li>\n</ul>\nThis ensures workshops translate into action.', 'Advisory Services', 'Our India risk and transaction advisory supports European and global companies with dispute resolution, compliance and internal audits, forensic reviews, financial due diligence, SAP and IT solutions, and cross-border transaction structuring through practical, governance-aligned support for Indian operations.', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '128-autosave-v1', '', '', '2026-03-11 15:18:59', '2026-03-11 14:18:59', '', 128, 'https://feboko.com/?p=182', 0, 'revision', '', 0),
