	(309, 4, '2026-07-07 14:51:28', '2026-07-07 12:51:28', '<h2>Backoffice Support with Structure, Continuity and Scalability</h2>\r\nFor many CPA firms, growth is limited not by demand, but by capacity. Tax season pressure, staff shortages, high local hiring costs and recurring administrative work often prevent firms from accepting additional clients or expanding their service offering.\r\n\r\nFeBoKo helps U.S. CPA firms build reliable offshore capacity without creating their own entity, hiring locally in India or managing an anonymous outsourcing pool. We provide dedicated professionals who are assigned to your firm, trained on your workflows and integrated into your existing tools and review processes.\r\n\r\nOur approach is based on continuity. Instead of constantly changing staff, FeBoKo focuses on long-term assignment, process familiarity and clear communication. This allows your firm to build a stable backoffice extension that understands your clients, your systems and your quality expectations over time.\r\n<h3>Our focus areas</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Dedicated backoffice teams for U.S. CPA and tax firms</li>\r\n 	<li>Accounting, bookkeeping, payroll and tax preparation support</li>\r\n 	<li>Firm-specific onboarding into tools, workflows and templates</li>\r\n 	<li>Scalable capacity during tax season and growth phases</li>\r\n 	<li>Backoffice execution while the CPA firm retains client ownership and final review control</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3>Our strengths</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>India-based accounting professionals with structured delivery discipline</li>\r\n 	<li>Dedicated staff model instead of constantly changing outsourced resources</li>\r\n 	<li>Strong process orientation and clear communication routines</li>\r\n 	<li>Flexible capacity that can be expanded or reduced with reasonable lead time</li>\r\n 	<li>Cross-border operating experience between Western clients and Indian execution teams</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h2>Accounting and Bookkeeping Support</h2>\r\nReliable accounting support requires more than data entry. CPA firms need clean reconciliations, properly prepared workpapers, accurate transaction categorisation and timely month-end support that fits into their existing review process.\r\n\r\nFeBoKo supports firms with recurring accounting and bookkeeping tasks that can be performed efficiently in the background while the U.S. firm remains responsible for client communication, review and advisory decisions. Our team works inside the firm’s existing workflow and prepares files, reports and reconciliations for review by the CPA firm.\r\n\r\nThis allows partners and senior staff to spend less time on repetitive operational tasks and more time on client advisory, review, relationship management and firm growth.\r\n<h3>Our focus areas</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Transaction categorisation and bookkeeping support</li>\r\n 	<li>Bank and credit card reconciliations</li>\r\n 	<li>Accounts payable and accounts receivable support</li>\r\n 	<li>Month-end close preparation</li>\r\n 	<li>Financial statement preparation support</li>\r\n 	<li>Trial balance and workpaper preparation</li>\r\n 	<li>Cleanup bookkeeping and recurring reporting support</li>\r\n 	<li>Support in common accounting systems based on the firm’s existing tools</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3>Our strengths</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Structured preparation of accounting work for U.S. firm review</li>\r\n 	<li>Continuity through dedicated team members</li>\r\n 	<li>Clear documentation of recurring workflows</li>\r\n 	<li>Practical support for small business and recurring client work</li>\r\n 	<li>Reduced operational pressure for partners, managers and local staff</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h2>Payroll Support</h2>\r\nPayroll is a recurring, deadline-driven process that requires accuracy, consistency and clear information flow. For many CPA firms, payroll support creates ongoing administrative pressure, especially when client information is incomplete, timesheets need clarification or payroll reports must be prepared on tight timelines.\r\n\r\nFeBoKo supports CPA firms with payroll-related backoffice preparation. Our role is to help collect, organise, reconcile and prepare payroll information so that the U.S. firm can review and finalise the process within its own compliance and client-service framework.\r\n\r\nWe do not replace the professional judgment of the CPA firm. Instead, we create structured operational support that makes recurring payroll work easier to manage and scale.\r\n<h3>Our focus areas</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Payroll data collection and organisation</li>\r\n 	<li>Timesheet reconciliation</li>\r\n 	<li>Payroll register preparation support</li>\r\n 	<li>Employee data checks and payroll information review</li>\r\n 	<li>Payroll journal entry preparation</li>\r\n 	<li>Payroll reporting support</li>\r\n 	<li>Missing information tracking</li>\r\n 	<li>Support for recurring payroll workflows in the firm’s existing systems</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3>Our strengths</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Consistent support for recurring payroll processes</li>\r\n 	<li>Clear handover and review-ready preparation</li>\r\n 	<li>Reduced administrative burden for U.S. teams</li>\r\n 	<li>Ability to support recurring client portfolios</li>\r\n 	<li>Structured communication around deadlines and missing information</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h2>Tax Preparation Support</h2>\r\nTax season creates significant operational pressure for CPA firms. Document collection, workpaper preparation, data entry, draft return preparation and missing-information follow-ups consume valuable time that could otherwise be used for review, client advisory and firm management.\r\n\r\nFeBoKo provides tax preparation support under the supervision and review of the U.S. CPA firm. Our team prepares documents, workpapers, draft returns and supporting schedules according to the firm’s instructions, templates and software environment.\r\n\r\nThe CPA firm retains responsibility for review, advice, signing, filing and client communication. FeBoKo works in the background to increase throughput, reduce bottlenecks and help the firm manage seasonal peaks more effectively.\r\n<h3>Our focus areas</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Tax document organisation</li>\r\n 	<li>Tax workpaper preparation</li>\r\n 	<li>Data entry into the firm’s tax software</li>\r\n 	<li>Draft preparation support for individual and business tax returns</li>\r\n 	<li>Support for 1040, 1120, 1120-S and 1065 workflows</li>\r\n 	<li>Schedule C, Schedule E and K-1 processing support</li>\r\n 	<li>Depreciation schedule preparation support</li>\r\n 	<li>Trial balance to tax return mapping</li>\r\n 	<li>Missing-information lists for client follow-up</li>\r\n 	<li>First-level self-review before CPA firm review</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3>Our strengths</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Support designed around CPA review and control</li>\r\n 	<li>Scalable capacity for tax season</li>\r\n 	<li>Clear separation between preparation support and final professional responsibility</li>\r\n 	<li>Dedicated staff trained on firm-specific return preparation workflows</li>\r\n 	<li>Practical relief for partners and reviewers during peak workload periods</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h2>Tax Filing Preparation Support</h2>\r\nFiling readiness depends on completeness, accuracy, documentation and review discipline. Even when the final filing decision remains with the CPA firm, a significant amount of preparatory work is required before a return is ready for final approval.\r\n\r\nFeBoKo supports firms in preparing filing-ready packages, organising supporting documentation and tracking the status of returns or client information. Our role is to help the U.S. firm move work from raw information to review-ready and filing-ready status with greater efficiency.\r\n\r\nThis service is especially valuable for firms that want better visibility across tax season workflows, clearer status tracking and more structured preparation before final CPA review.\r\n<h3>Our focus areas</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Preparation of filing-ready workpapers</li>\r\n 	<li>Assembly of draft tax return packages</li>\r\n 	<li>Review of completeness before CPA approval</li>\r\n 	<li>Supporting schedule preparation</li>\r\n 	<li>Client document request lists</li>\r\n 	<li>Status tracking for return preparation workflows</li>\r\n 	<li>E-filing package preparation for CPA firm review</li>\r\n 	<li>Coordination of missing documents and open items</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3>Our strengths</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Structured preparation before final CPA approval</li>\r\n 	<li>Better visibility across tax workflow status</li>\r\n 	<li>Reduced last-minute bottlenecks</li>\r\n 	<li>Clear documentation of open items and missing information</li>\r\n 	<li>Support that keeps filing control with the U.S. firm</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h2>Dedicated Team Model</h2>\r\nFeBoKo’s core differentiator is the dedicated team model. Many outsourcing arrangements fail because firms receive changing staff, inconsistent communication and repeated onboarding effort. FeBoKo addresses this by assigning professionals to specific CPA firms and building process familiarity over time.\r\n\r\nYour dedicated FeBoKo team learns your tools, templates, client types, internal review expectations and communication preferences. As the relationship develops, the team becomes more efficient, reduces repeated explanations and provides a more stable extension of your internal capacity.\r\n\r\nWhen your workload increases, additional capacity can be added with reasonable lead time. When your workload decreases after tax season, capacity can be adjusted. This gives your firm more flexibility than local hiring while preserving more continuity than traditional outsourcing models.\r\n<h3>Our focus areas</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Dedicated professionals assigned to your firm</li>\r\n 	<li>Firm-specific onboarding and process documentation</li>\r\n 	<li>Flexible capacity planning for tax season and growth phases</li>\r\n 	<li>Team lead coordination and escalation structure</li>\r\n 	<li>Backup planning for continuity</li>\r\n 	<li>Regular performance and workflow review</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3>Our strengths</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Continuity instead of anonymous task outsourcing</li>\r\n 	<li>Lower onboarding friction over time</li>\r\n 	<li>Clear responsibility and communication channels</li>\r\n 	<li>Scalable team structures from individual support to backoffice pods</li>\r\n 	<li>Strong fit for CPA firms that want long-term offshore capacity without building their own India operation</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h2>Pilot and Onboarding Process</h2>\r\nSuccessful offshore support starts with a structured onboarding process. FeBoKo does not simply assign staff and begin work without understanding the firm’s workflows. We first clarify the scope, tools, review process, client types, communication routines and quality expectations.\r\n\r\nA pilot can be used to test selected workflows before expanding into a dedicated long-term model. This gives the CPA firm a low-risk way to evaluate quality, communication and operational fit.\r\n\r\nAfter the pilot, FeBoKo and the CPA firm can define a scalable team structure based on actual workload, seasonal demand and long-term growth objectives.\r\n<h3>Our focus areas</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Initial workflow and capacity assessment</li>\r\n 	<li>Definition of suitable backoffice tasks</li>\r\n 	<li>Tool and process onboarding</li>\r\n 	<li>Pilot setup with defined scope and deliverables</li>\r\n 	<li>Weekly review calls during the pilot phase</li>\r\n 	<li>Quality feedback and workflow improvement</li>\r\n 	<li>Expansion into a dedicated accountant or dedicated team model</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3>Our strengths</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Structured implementation instead of unplanned outsourcing</li>\r\n 	<li>Clear expectations before operational work begins</li>\r\n 	<li>Practical pilot model for first-time offshore users</li>\r\n 	<li>Focus on measurable output, quality and communication</li>\r\n 	<li>Long-term scalability based on proven workflows</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h2>FeBoKo as Your Backoffice Partner</h2>\r\nFeBoKo combines India-based operational capacity with a structured, client-oriented delivery model. We understand that CPA firms do not only need lower costs. They need reliability, confidentiality, continuity, quality and control.\r\n\r\nOur role is to support your firm in the background while you remain the client-facing advisor. Whether you need recurring bookkeeping support, payroll preparation, tax season capacity or a dedicated long-term backoffice team, FeBoKo helps you build capacity in a structured and scalable way.\r\n\r\nWe are particularly suited for CPA firms that want to grow without increasing local hiring pressure, improve margins without compromising control and create a more resilient operating model for recurring accounting and tax work.\r\n<h3>Our focus areas</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Dedicated backoffice support for U.S. CPA firms</li>\r\n 	<li>Accounting, payroll and tax preparation workflows</li>\r\n 	<li>Scalable India-based execution capacity</li>\r\n 	<li>Long-term team continuity</li>\r\n 	<li>Support under the supervision and review of the U.S. firm</li>\r\n 	<li>Practical operating model for growth and tax season relief</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3>Our strengths</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Dedicated staff instead of rotating outsourced resources</li>\r\n 	<li>Strong India execution capabilities</li>\r\n 	<li>Cross-border business understanding</li>\r\n 	<li>Flexible capacity model</li>\r\n 	<li>Process-oriented onboarding and delivery</li>\r\n 	<li>Clear focus on supporting, not replacing, the CPA firm’s professional role</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h2>Typical Engagement Models</h2>\r\nFeBoKo offers flexible engagement models depending on the firm’s workload, growth plans and desired level of support.\r\n<h3>Backoffice Pilot</h3>\r\nA structured pilot for CPA firms that want to test selected workflows before committing to a long-term model.\r\n\r\nTypical use cases include bookkeeping support, tax document organisation, workpaper preparation or selected recurring accounting tasks.\r\n<h3>Dedicated Accountant</h3>\r\nA dedicated FeBoKo professional assigned to your firm for ongoing accounting, bookkeeping, payroll or tax preparation support.\r\n\r\nThis model is suitable for firms that need stable recurring capacity and want the same person to become familiar with their workflows.\r\n<h3>Tax Season Capacity</h3>\r\nAdditional preparation support during peak tax season.\r\n\r\nThis model is suitable for firms that need temporary capacity for document organisation, workpaper preparation, draft returns and status tracking.\r\n<h3>Dedicated Backoffice Pod</h3>\r\nA scalable team structure for growing CPA firms that need a broader operational extension across accounting, payroll and tax preparation workflows.\r\n\r\nThis model can include junior staff, senior preparers and an India-based team lead.\r\n<h2>How We Work</h2>\r\nOur collaboration model is designed to keep the CPA firm in control while reducing operational workload.\r\n<ol>\r\n 	<li>We assess your workflows, tools and capacity needs.</li>\r\n 	<li>We define suitable backoffice tasks and responsibilities.</li>\r\n 	<li>We onboard dedicated FeBoKo professionals into your process.</li>\r\n 	<li>We document recurring workflows and review expectations.</li>\r\n 	<li>We prepare accounting, payroll or tax-related work for your team’s review.</li>\r\n 	<li>Your firm retains client communication, professional judgment, final review and filing responsibility.</li>\r\n 	<li>We adjust capacity as your workload changes.</li>\r\n</ol>\r\nThis creates a practical operating model for firms that want to scale without losing control.\r\n<h2>Build Scalable Backoffice Capacity with FeBoKo</h2>\r\nFeBoKo helps U.S. CPA firms increase capacity, reduce operational pressure and improve margins through dedicated India-based backoffice teams.\r\n\r\nIf your firm wants to accept more clients, manage tax season more effectively or build a more scalable operating model for recurring accounting and tax work, FeBoKo can support you with structured, dedicated and flexible backoffice capacity.', 'Backoffice Solutions for U.S. CPA Firms', 'FeBoKo supports U.S. CPA firms and tax practices with dedicated India-based backoffice teams for accounting, bookkeeping, payroll support, tax preparation support and tax filing preparation. Our model is designed for firms that want to increase capacity, improve margins and reduce operational pressure while keeping full control over client relationships, review responsibility and final filing decisions.', 'publish', 'closed', 'closed', '', 'backoffice-solutions-cpa-firms', '', '', '2026-07-07 14:51:28', '2026-07-07 12:51:28', '', 0, 'https://feboko.com/?post_type=service&#038;p=309', 11, 'service', '', 0),
